+{"timestamp":"2026-11-01T20:42:47.917Z","ordinal":39,"type":"token_usage_record","payload":{"thread_id":"01a198d9-52a2-7b63-b71b-a496f3202e83","turn_id":"01a198d9-52cd-7300-bac5-f48f3b1e760b","session_id":"01a198cb-beb8-7583-ac3f-b9987979ebc5","root_turn_id":"01a198cb-c037-7263-8906-ad8972ad8353","response_id":"resp_06e1c13127810fc2016ae7a4443414819195be9f8fe2ebb9c0","usage":{"input_tokens":42361,"cached_input_tokens":35072,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":116,"reasoning_output_tokens":47,"total_tokens":42477},"turn_token_usage":{"input_tokens":137764,"cached_input_tokens":122240,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":800,"reasoning_output_tokens":378,"total_tokens":138564},"thread_token_usage":{"input_tokens":137764,"cached_input_tokens":122240,"cache_write_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":800,"reasoning_output_tokens":378,"total_tokens":138564}}}
+{"timestamp":"2026-11-01T20:42:47.983Z","ordinal":40,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a198d9-52a2-7b63-b71b-a496f3202e83","turn_id":"01a198d9-52cd-7300-bac5-f48f3b1e760b","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-7ebae0ad-099b-41b9-a989-4847177e3de7","process_id":"65125","command":["/opt/homebrew/bin/bash","-lc","python3 -c 'import subprocess; subprocess.run([\"rg\", \"-n\", \"-m\", \"55\", \"^\", \"CHANGELOG.md\"], timeout=60, check=True)'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/gems","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python3 -c 'import subprocess; subprocess.run([\"rg\", \"-n\", \"-m\", \"55\", \"^\", \"CHANGELOG.md\"], timeout=60, check=True)'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"1:# Changelog\n2:\n3:All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.\n4:\n5:The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/),\n6:and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).\n7:\n8:## [Unreleased]\n9:\n10:### Added\n11:\n12:- **backup**: `--jobs` controls concurrent archive instances (default three); cancellation stops new work, joins workers, stops tar and cleans temporary files while preserving completed results and backups; interruption exits with status 130.\n13:- **backup**: `--plan` previews metadata-only run/skip/fail decisions, reasons and existing-output replacement markers; selected outputs share one timestamp and colliding paths are rejected before plan, run or dry-run execution.\n14:- **backup**: optional `items` bundle literal source-relative files and directories into one archive, preserving empty directories and symlinks while applying inherited exclusions and `.bkpignore` rules.\n15:- **backup**: per-instance `inherit_excludes`, `exclude_remove` and `exclude_add` control inherited exclusions for archives and `--show-excludes`.\n16:\n17:### Changed\n18:\n19:- **backup**: missing sources and bundles with no surviving members now warn and skip without touching previous archives; each run reports archived or previewed, skipped, and failed step counts. Existing non-directory sources and unreadable selected files still fail.\n20:\n21:### Fixed\n22:\n23:- **backup**: interruption during submission or result collection preserves every instance's outcome and finishes cleanup without waiting for a lost completion notification.\n24:- **backup**: a source or output metadata error while planning one instance now fails only that instance; the others still run, and duplicate outputs are still rejected.\n25:- **backup**: `tar-archive` plans treat an empty `engine` as the default Python engine and report an empty `source` or `out` as \"no source configured\" or \"no out path configured\", the same as a run, instead of using the working directory; two instances with an empty `out` no longer report a false output collision.\n26:- **sysup**: a `timeout` on a captured multi-command shell step now stops the whole step; before, only bash died and the command it was waiting on kept running. Such a step runs in its own process group, so Ctrl-C is forwarded to it, a terminal prompt it raises stops it until the timeout, and a command it runs as root through `sudo` is still out of reach and survives. Interactive steps and steps without a timeout are unchanged\n27:\n28:## [0.16.0] - 2026-10-29\n29:\n30:### Added\n31:\n32:- **sysup**: a step in a run entry, and a refresh command, may be written as a plain shell line such as `HOMEBREW_NO_UPGRADE_AUTO_UPDATES_CASKS=1 brew upgrade --quiet`, run by `bash -eo pipefail -c`, so variables, pipes, `&&` and `VAR=1 cmd` prefixes work as typed and a failing command anywhere in a pipe fails the step; an argv array still runs without a shell, and either may be an `{argv, env}` object whose `env` is merged over the parent environment for that step only (`~` expanded). An empty step is rejected when the config loads instead of failing mid-run\n33:\n34:### Changed\n35:\n36:- **sysup**: the bundled entries are written as shell lines; `brew` upgrades with `HOMEBREW_NO_UPGRADE_AUTO_UPDATES_CASKS=1` and `--quiet`, leaving self-updating casks to their own updater; sudo priming triggers on any step that invokes `sudo`, not only one whose argv starts with it\n37:\n38:## [0.15.3] - 2026-10-28\n39:\n40:### Fixed\n41:\n42:- **sysup**: the bundled `brew upgrade` passes `--no-ask`, so Homebrew no longer stops the run with a \"Do you want to proceed with the upgrade?\" prompt now that the step is interactive\n43:- **sysup**: the pipx-python step also walks `config.local.toml` beside the mise config, so pipx tools kept in the machine-local file follow the global python minor bump too\n44:\n45:## [0.15.2] - 2026-10-28\n46:\n47:### Fixed\n48:\n49:- **sysup**: the bundled `brew` step runs interactively, so the sudo password prompt Homebrew raises for casks is visible instead of hiding behind the spinner and freezing the run\n50:\n51:## [0.15.1] - 2026-10-27\n52:\n53:### Fixed\n54:\n55:- **sysup**: `uv-tool-python` now moves editable and otherwise customized uv tool installs with `uv tool upgrade --python`, so a host with an editable tool no longer ends every run red; only malformed receipts are skipped; tools already on the global minor are left alone, and a failed move restores the receipt uv deleted before rolling back\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":7709}},"started_at_ms":1793565767983,"completed_at_ms":1793565767983}}
+{"timestamp":"2026-11-01T20:42:47.985Z","ordinal":41,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a198d9-b931-77f2-bd2e-e885dc0d8414","call_id":"call_964d1caf616e4dc0b3d818ddf7d48ee0","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"28fea4\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000007709,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":1136,\"output\":\"1:# Changelog\\n2:\\n3:All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.\\n4:\\n5:The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/),\\n6:and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).\\n7:\\n8:## [Unreleased]\\n9:\\n10:### Added\\n11:\\n12:- **backup**: `--jobs` controls concurrent archive instances (default three); cancellation stops new work, joins workers, stops tar and cleans temporary files while preserving completed results and backups; interruption exits with status 130.\\n13:- **backup**: `--plan` previews metadata-only run/skip/fail decisions, reasons and existing-output replacement markers; selected outputs share one timestamp and colliding paths are rejected before plan, run or dry-run execution.\\n14:- **backup**: optional `items` bundle literal source-relative files and directories into one archive, preserving empty directories and symlinks while applying inherited exclusions and `.bkpignore` rules.\\n15:- **backup**: per-instance `inherit_excludes`, `exclude_remove` and `exclude_add` control inherited exclusions for archives and `--show-excludes`.\\n16:\\n17:### Changed\\n18:\\n19:- **backup**: missing sources and bundles with no surviving members now warn and skip without touching previous archives; each run reports archived or previewed, skipped, and failed step counts. Existing non-directory sources and unreadable selected files still fail.\\n20:\\n21:### Fixed\\n22:\\n23:- **backup**: interruption during submission or result collection preserves every instance's outcome and finishes cleanup without waiting for a lost completion notification.\\n24:- **backup**: a source or output metadata error while planning one instance now fails only that instance; the others still run, and duplicate outputs are still rejected.\\n25:- **backup**: `tar-archive` plans treat an empty `engine` as the default Python engine and report an empty `source` or `out` as \\\"no source configured\\\" or \\\"no out path configured\\\", the same as a run, instead of using the working directory; two instances with an empty `out` no longer report a false output collision.\\n26:- **sysup**: a `timeout` on a captured multi-command shell step now stops the whole step; before, only bash died and the command it was waiting on kept running. Such a step runs in its own process group, so Ctrl-C is forwarded to it, a terminal prompt it raises stops it until the timeout, and a command it runs as root through `sudo` is still out of reach and survives. Interactive steps and steps without a timeout are unchanged\\n27:\\n28:## [0.16.0] - 2026-10-29\\n29:\\n30:### Added\\n31:\\n32:- **sysup**: a step in a run entry, and a refresh command, may be written as a plain shell line such as `HOMEBREW_NO_UPGRADE_AUTO_UPDATES_CASKS=1 brew upgrade --quiet`, run by `bash -eo pipefail -c`, so variables, pipes, `&&` and `VAR=1 cmd` prefixes work as typed and a failing command anywhere in a pipe fails the step; an argv array still runs without a shell, and either may be an `{argv, env}` object whose `env` is merged over the parent environment for that step only (`~` expanded). An empty step is rejected when the config loads instead of failing mid-run\\n33:\\n34:### Changed\\n35:\\n36:- **sysup**: the bundled entries are written as shell lines; `brew` upgrades with `HOMEBREW_NO_UPGRADE_AUTO_UPDATES_CASKS=1` and `--quiet`, leaving self-updating casks to their own updater; sudo priming triggers on any step that invokes `sudo`, not only one whose argv starts with it\\n37:\\n38:## [0.15.3] - 2026-10-28\\n39:\\n40:### Fixed\\n41:\\n42:- **sysup**: the bundled `brew upgrade` passes `--no-ask`, so Homebrew no longer stops the run with a \\\"Do you want to proceed with the upgrade?\\\" prompt now that the step is interactive\\n43:- **sysup**: the pipx-python step also walks `config.local.toml` beside the mise config, so pipx tools kept in the machine-local file follow the global python minor bump too\\n44:\\n45:## [0.15.2] - 2026-10-28\\n46:\\n47:### Fixed\\n48:\\n49:- **sysup**: the bundled `brew` step runs interactively, so the sudo password prompt Homebrew raises for casks is visible instead of hiding behind the spinner and freezing the run\\n50:\\n51:## [0.15.1] - 2026-10-27\\n52:\\n53:### Fixed\\n54:\\n55:- **sysup**: `uv-tool-python` now moves editable and otherwise customized uv tool installs with `uv tool upgrade --python`, so a host with an editable tool no longer ends every run red; only malformed receipts are skipped; tools already on the global minor are left alone, and a failed move restores the receipt uv deleted before rolling back\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a198d9-52cd-7300-bac5-f48f3b1e760b","create_time":1793565767.985926}},"metadata":{"client_authored":false,"fallback_token_limit_override":12000}}
