stream. Existing raw-file flush, fsync, mode 0600, cancellation checks, atomic `os.replace` and `BaseException` temp cleanup remain in their current order. A finalizing event means the stream closed, not that publication succeeded; the terminal `StepResult` remains authoritative.\n\nFor the configured system-tar engine, `done_bytes` is `None` for every archiving/finalizing event. A failed system attempt followed by the existing Python fallback retains this activity-only policy for the instance: pass no `on_bytes` callback to the fallback writer, but preserve finalizing and the existing fallback note. This avoids changing percentage semantics partway through a configured system-tar job. No subprocess output parsing or archive-size polling is introduced.\nRead-only support modules: /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/gems/src/tools/backup/step_result.py, /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/gems/src/tools/backup/config.py, /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/gems/src/tools/backup/capabilities/__init__.py, /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/gems/src/tools/backup/runner.py\nREADING BUDGET: Read tar_archive.py lines1-235 for runtime kwargs and validated/result paths, lines405-495 for writers. Other walk helpers need only signatures unless a test fails there. Ordered work: (1) safe emitter and validated phase hooks; (2) Python writer input accounting and successful-close callback, test byte cases; (3) system writer close callback/fallback activity semantics, test engine/callback cases; (4) focused changelog entry. Preserve original write durability and cancellation checks. Avoid rereading entire600-line source.\n\nUse Python patterns at /Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md for Python edits. Keep modified functions under50 lines and Python files under800 lines, preserving behavior; small helpers within allowlisted source are permitted. Existing task tests are read-only. Add a focused Added CHANGELOG entry under Unreleased for this task; it is mandatory in eac