+{"timestamp":"2026-11-01T20:47:41.539Z","ordinal":24,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a198de-0530-7022-ab77-ebc7e796bc9b","turn_id":"01a198de-0551-7673-85dd-5e15589d93ba","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a1e91e92-a59d-4a2b-9f85-e325cb30f041","process_id":"44722","command":["/opt/homebrew/bin/bash","-lc","python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor path in [Path('/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md'),Path('/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md'),Path('tests/tools/backup/test_progress.py')]:\n    print(f'FILE: {path}')\n    print(path.read_text())\nPY"],"cwd":"file:///Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/gems","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor path in [Path('/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md'),Path('/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md'),Path('tests/tools/backup/test_progress.py')]:\n    print(f'FILE: {path}')\n    print(path.read_text())\nPY"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"FILE: /Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md\n---\nname: python-testing\ndescription: Use when writing, fixing, or reviewing Python tests with pytest. Covers TDD, fixtures, mocking, parametrization, coverage. Triggers on \"pytest\", \"python test\", \"conftest\", \"pytest.mark\", \"parametrize\", \"pytest fixture\", \"python mock\".\ncompatibility: \"Portable standalone compatibility copy of the strunk plugin skill for agents without that plugin; Claude Code uses the namespaced plugin skill.\"\n---\n\n# Python Testing\n\nTDD: write the failing test (RED), make it pass (GREEN), refactor. One behavior per test. No logic in tests. Coverage target 80%, higher on critical paths.\n\n## Rulings\n\n**Mocking**\n- Patch where the name is *used*, not where it's defined: `@patch(\"myapp.service.requests\")`, not `@patch(\"requests\")`.\n- `autospec=True` so the mock rejects calls the real API would reject.\n- Mock at the boundary (I/O, network, clock). Never mock the thing under test.\n- Async: assert with `assert_awaited_once()`, not `assert_called_once()`.\n\n**Fixtures**\n- `yield` for teardown; the line after `yield` is the cleanup.\n- Default to function scope. Widen to `module`/`session` only for genuinely expensive resources.\n- `autouse` hides dependencies — use sparingly; prefer explicit injection.\n- `tmp_path` for temp files (auto-cleanup, `Path` API), not `tempfile`.\n\n**Parametrize**\n- `@pytest.mark.parametrize` over loops — distinct test IDs, filterable with `-k`.\n- Pass `ids=[...]` when params are objects or tuples; pytest already auto-names plain str/int/bool readably.\n\n**Config**\n- One config in `pyproject.toml` (`[tool.pytest.ini_options]`), not a separate `pytest.ini`.\n- `--strict-markers` so a typo'd marker fails instead of silently passing.\n- Register custom markers — e.g. `slow`, `@pytest.mark.unit`, `@pytest.mark.integration` — so `--strict-markers` catches a typo.\n- Coverage locally: `pytest --cov=src --cov-report=term-missing` — the missing-line report is the point; a bare percentage is not actionable.\n\n**Async (pytest-asyncio)**\n- Default mode is `strict`: an async test with no `@pytest.mark.asyncio` is silently not collected. Set `asyncio_mode = \"auto\"` in `[tool.pytest.ini_options]` to drop the per-test marker.\n- Use `@pytest_asyncio.fixture` for async fixtures in strict mode.\n\nFILE: /Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md\n---\nname: python-patterns\ndescription: Use when writing, reviewing, or refactoring Python code. Covers idioms, naming, traps, toolchain, and security. Triggers on Python file edits, \"pythonic\", \"PEP 8\", \"python best practices\", \"python idioms\", \"bandit\".\ncompatibility: \"Portable standalone compatibility copy of the strunk plugin skill for agents without that plugin; Claude Code uses the namespaced plugin skill.\"\n---\n\n# Python Patterns\n\nPick a side. These are the rulings, not a tutorial.\n\n## Idioms that earn their place\n\n| Rule | Why |\n|------|-----|\n| `X \\| Y`, not `Union[X, Y]` | 3.10+ runtime syntax; clearer. On 3.9 it parses only under `from __future__ import annotations` and still breaks `get_type_hints`/`isinstance` — keep `Optional`/`Union` if you support 3.9. |\n| `Protocol`, not `ABC`, for duck typing | Structural typing; no inheritance you don't control. |\n| `@dataclass(frozen=True)` for immutable records, plain `dataclass` only when you must mutate, `NamedTuple` for lightweight immutable rows | Pydantic only when you need validation. |\n| `raise New(...) from e` | Marks the explicit cause. A bare `raise New()` still chains implicitly (\"During handling...\"); use `from None` to suppress. |\n| `@functools.wraps` on every decorator | Without it the wrapper loses `__name__`, `__doc__`, signature. |\n| `pathlib.Path`, not `os.path` | One object, no string surgery. |\n\n## Naming (PEP 8)\n\n`snake_case` for modules, functions, variables. `CapWords` for classes. `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` for constants. Leading `_` for internal names.\n\n**Never name a `.py` file in kebab-case.** `my-script.py` is not importable (`import my-script` is a `SyntaxError`). Kebab-case belongs only in the `pyproject.toml` distribution name and the CLI command, both of which map to a `snake_case` module.\n\n## Traps\n\n```python\n# Mutable default argument — shared across calls\ndef bad(items=[]): ...\ndef good(items=None):\n    items = [] if items is None else items\n\n# Bare except — swallows SystemExit, KeyboardInterrupt\ntry: ...\nexcept Exception as e: ...        # name the exception\n\n# __slots__ kills __dict__ and dynamic attributes — use only on fixed,\n# memory-sensitive classes you won't extend.\n\n# __double_leading is name-mangled to _Class__double_leading.\n# Surprises you in subclasses, pickling, and monkey-patching.\n\nif value is None: ...             # never == None\n```\n\nAvoid `from module import *`. Use `isinstance`, never `type(x) ==`.\n\n## Toolchain\n\n**black** to format, **isort** for imports, **ruff** to lint. Type annotations on every function signature — no exceptions for \"obvious\" returns.\n\n## Resources and laziness\n\nContext managers (`with`) for anything holding a resource. Generators for lazy iteration over anything you would otherwise materialize into a list.\n\n## Security\n\n- Read secrets with `os.environ[\"API_KEY\"]`, never `.get()` — a missing secret must raise `KeyError` at startup, not surface as `None` at request time.\n- `python-dotenv` loads a local `.env` in development only. Never commit one.\n- `bandit -r src/` for static security analysis.\n\nFILE: tests/tools/backup/test_progress.py\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport os\nimport tarfile\nimport threading\nimport time\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Literal, get_type_hints\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom backup.capabilities import tar_archive\nfrom backup.capabilities.tar_archive import TarArchive, _write_archive\nfrom backup.step_result import ProgressEvent\n\n\nclass TestProgressEventRecord:\n    def test_event_record_has_exact_named_tuple_fields_types_and_no_defaults(self) -> None:\n        assert ProgressEvent.__bases__ == (tuple,)\n        assert ProgressEvent._fields == (\"label\", \"phase\", \"done_bytes\", \"total_bytes\")\n        assert ProgressEvent._field_defaults == {}\n        assert get_type_hints(ProgressEvent) == {\n            \"label\": str,\n            \"phase\": Literal[\"scanning\", \"archiving\", \"finalizing\"],\n            \"done_bytes\": int | None,\n            \"total_bytes\": int | None,\n        }\n\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\n        \"label,phase,done_bytes,total_bytes\",\n        [\n            (\"documents\", \"scanning\", None, None),\n            (\"documents-old\", \"archiving\", 37, 101),\n            (\"\", \"finalizing\", 0, 0),\n            (\"photos\", \"archiving\", 2**40, 2**41),\n            (\"photos\", \"scanning\", 0, None),\n            (\"documents\", \"finalizing\", None, 101),\n            (\"Příliš žluťoučký 🗃️\", \"archiving\", 2**63, 2**80),\n        ],\n    )\n    def test_event_record_preserves_each_positional_field_and_byte_value(\n        self,\n        label: str,\n        phase: Literal[\"scanning\", \"archiving\", \"finalizing\"],\n        done_bytes: int | None,\n        total_bytes: int | None,\n    ) -> None:\n        event = ProgressEvent(label, phase, done_bytes, total_bytes)\n        assert event.label == label\n        assert event.phase == phase\n        assert event.done_bytes == done_bytes\n        assert event.total_bytes == total_bytes\n        assert event[0] == event.label\n        assert event[1] == event.phase\n        assert event[2] == event.done_bytes\n        assert event[3] == event.total_bytes\n        assert tuple(event) == (label, phase, done_bytes, total_bytes)\n        assert event == ProgressEvent(\n            total_bytes=total_bytes,\n            done_bytes=done_bytes,\n            phase=phase,\n            label=label,\n        )\n        assert event == ProgressEvent(label, phase=phase, done_bytes=done_bytes, total_bytes=total_bytes)\n\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"field\", [\"label\", \"phase\", \"done_bytes\", \"total_bytes\"])\n    def test_event_record_rejects_field_mutation(self, field: str) -> None:\n        event = ProgressEvent(\"documents\", \"archiving\", 37, 101)\n        assert not hasattr(event, \"__dict__\")\n        with pytest.raises(AttributeError):\n            setattr(event, field, None)\n        assert tuple(event) == (\"documents\", \"archiving\", 37, 101)\n\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\n        \"args\",\n        [(), (\"documents\",), (\"documents\", \"scanning\"), (\"documents\", \"scanning\", None)],\n    )\n    def test_event_record_requires_all_four_arguments(self, args: tuple[object, ...]) -> None:\n        with pytest.raises(TypeError):\n            ProgressEvent(*args)\n\n    def test_event_record_distinguishes_similar_labels_and_each_field(self) -> None:\n        event = ProgressEvent(\"documents\", \"archiving\", 37, 101)\n        assert event != ProgressEvent(\"documents-old\", \"archiving\", 37, 101)\n        assert event != ProgressEvent(\"documents\", \"finalizing\", 37, 101)\n        assert event != ProgressEvent(\"documents\", \"archiving\", 38, 101)\n        assert event != ProgressEvent(\"documents\", \"archiving\", 37, 102)\n\n    def test_event_record_crosses_worker_thread_without_sharing_mutable_call_state(self) -> None:\n        original = ProgressEvent(\"documents\", \"scanning\", None, None)\n\n        def update_in_worker(event: ProgressEvent) -> tuple[ProgressEvent, ProgressEvent]:\n            updated = event._replace(phase=\"archiving\", done_bytes=37, total_bytes=101)\n            other = ProgressEvent(\"photos\", \"finalizing\", 0, 0)\n            return updated, other\n\n        with ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=1) as executor:\n            updated, other = executor.submit(update_in_worker, original).result(timeout=5)\n        assert tuple(original) == (\"documents\", \"scanning\", None, None)\n        assert (original.label, original.phase, original.done_bytes, original.total_bytes) == (\n            \"documents\",\n            \"scanning\",\n            None,\n            None,\n        )\n        assert (other.label, other.phase, other.done_bytes, other.total_bytes) == (\"photos\", \"finalizing\", 0, 0)\n        assert isinstance(updated, ProgressEvent)\n        assert tuple(updated) == (\"documents\", \"archiving\", 37, 101)\n        replacements = [\n            (original._replace(label=\"photos\"), (\"photos\", \"scanning\", None, None)),\n            (original._replace(phase=\"finalizing\"), (\"documents\", \"finalizing\", None, None)),\n            (original._replace(done_bytes=37), (\"documents\", \"scanning\", 37, None)),\n            (original._replace(total_bytes=101), (\"documents\", \"scanning\", None, 101)),\n            (updated._replace(done_bytes=None), (\"documents\", \"archiving\", None, 101)),\n            (updated._replace(total_bytes=None), (\"documents\", \"archiving\", 37, None)),\n        ]\n        for replacement, expected in replacements:\n            assert isinstance(replacement, ProgressEvent)\n            assert (\n                replacement.label,\n                replacement.phase,\n                replacement.done_bytes,\n                replacement.total_bytes,\n            ) == expected\n            assert tuple(replacement) == expected\n\n\nclass TestArchiveEngineProgress:\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"engine\", [\"python-tarfile\", \"system-tar\"])\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"label,sizes\", [(\"docs\", [7, 19]), (\"docs-old\", [11, 31])])\n    def test_engine_reports_ordered_phases_and_selected_input_bytes_before_publication(\n        self, tmp_path: Path, engine: str, label: str, sizes: list[int],\n    ) -> None:\n        source = tmp_path / \"src\"\n        source.mkdir()\n        for name, size in zip([\"a-old\", \"b\"], sizes, strict=True):\n            (source / name).write_bytes(b\"x\" * size)\n        (source / \"a\").write_bytes(b\"excluded\" * 13)\n        out = tmp_path / \"out.tar.gz\"\n        out.write_bytes(b\"previous archive\")\n        events: list[ProgressEvent] = []\n        finalizing_output: list[bytes] = []\n\n        def progress(event: ProgressEvent) -> None:\n            events.append(event)\n            if event.phase == \"finalizing\":\n                finalizing_output.append(out.read_bytes())\n\n        result = next(iter(TarArchive().run(\n            label=label, source=str(source), out=str(out), engine=engine,\n            items=[\"a\", \"a-old\", \"b\"], excludes=[\"a\"], progress=progress,\n        )))\n        assert result.success is True\n        assert finalizing_output == [b\"previous archive\"]\n        total = sum(sizes)\n        done = total if engine == \"python-tarfile\" else None\n        assert events[0] == ProgressEvent(label, \"scanning\", None, None)\n        assert events[1] == ProgressEvent(label, \"archiving\", 0 if done is not None else None, total)\n        assert events[-1] == ProgressEvent(label, \"finalizing\", done, total)\n        assert all(event.label == label for event in events)\n        assert all(event.total_bytes == total for event in events[1:])\n        assert all(event.phase == \"archiving\" for event in events[1:-1])\n        if engine == \"system-tar\":\n            assert all(event.done_bytes is None for event in events)\n        else:\n            assert events[-2] == ProgressEvent(label, \"archiving\", total, total)\n        with tarfile.open(out) as archive:\n            assert {Path(member.name).name for member in archive.getmembers() if member.isfile()} == {\"a-old\", \"b\"}\n        assert out.stat().st_mode & 0o777 == 0o600\n\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"sizes\", [[3, 7, 11, 17], [5, 13, 19, 23]])\n    def test_engine_throttles_at_two_tenths_and_flushes_short_final_count(\n        self, tmp_path: Path, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch, sizes: list[int],\n    ) -> None:\n        source = tmp_path / \"src\"\n        source.mkdir()\n        names = [\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\"]\n        for name, size in zip(names, sizes, strict=True):\n            (source / name).write_bytes(b\"x\" * size)\n        clock = [0.0]\n        moments = dict(zip(names, [0.199, 0.2, 0.399, 0.3999], strict=True))\n        original_add = tarfile.TarFile.add\n\n        def add_with_clock(archive: tarfile.TarFile, name: str, *args: object, **kwargs: object) -> None:\n            original_add(archive, name, *args, **kwargs)\n            clock[0] = moments[Path(name).name]\n\n        monkeypatch.setattr(time, \"monotonic\", lambda: clock[0])\n        monkeypatch.setattr(tarfile.TarFile, \"add\", add_with_clock)\n        events: list[ProgressEvent] = []\n        result = next(iter(TarArchive().run(\n            label=\"timed\", source=str(source), out=str(tmp_path / \"timed.tar.gz\"),\n            engine=\"python-tarfile\", items=names, progress=events.append,\n        )))\n        assert result.success is True\n        total = sum(sizes)\n        assert events == [\n            ProgressEvent(\"timed\", \"scanning\", None, None),\n            ProgressEvent(\"timed\", \"archiving\", 0, total),\n            ProgressEvent(\"timed\", \"archiving\", sum(sizes[:2]), total),\n            ProgressEvent(\"timed\", \"archiving\", total, total),\n            ProgressEvent(\"timed\", \"finalizing\", total, total),\n        ]\n\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"label,size\", [(\"first\", 7), (\"first-old\", 29)])\n    def test_engine_short_archive_flushes_without_waiting_or_duplicate_final_count(\n        self, tmp_path: Path, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch, label: str, size: int,\n    ) -> None:\n        source = tmp_path / \"src\"\n        source.mkdir()\n        (source / \"payload\").write_bytes(b\"x\" * size)\n        monkeypatch.setattr(time, \"monotonic\", lambda: 42.0)\n        events: list[ProgressEvent] = []\n        result = next(iter(TarArchive().run(\n            label=label, source=str(source), out=str(tmp_path / \"out.tar.gz\"),\n            engine=\"python-tarfile\", progress=events.append,\n        )))\n        assert result.success is True\n        assert events == [\n            ProgressEvent(label, \"scanning\", None, None),\n            ProgressEvent(label, \"archiving\", 0, size),\n            ProgressEvent(label, \"archiving\", size, size),\n            ProgressEvent(label, \"finalizing\", size, size),\n        ]\n\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"engine\", [\"python-tarfile\", \"system-tar\"])\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"items\", [None, [\"a\", \"b\"]])\n    def test_engine_direct_dry_run_never_calls_progress(\n        self, tmp_path: Path, engine: str, items: list[str] | None,\n    ) -> None:\n        source = tmp_path / \"src\"\n        source.mkdir()\n        (source / \"a\").write_bytes(b\"first\")\n        (source / \"b\").write_bytes(b\"second payload\")\n        out = tmp_path / \"out.tar.gz\"\n        events: list[ProgressEvent] = []\n        result = next(iter(TarArchive().run(\n            label=\"preview\", source=str(source), out=str(out), engine=engine,\n            items=items, dry_run=True, progress=events.append,\n        )))\n        assert result.success is True\n        assert events == []\n        assert not out.exists()\n\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"source_state\", [\"missing\", \"file\"])\n    def test_engine_unwalkable_source_emits_no_fabricated_activity(\n        self, tmp_path: Path, source_state: str,\n    ) -> None:\n        source = tmp_path / source_state\n        if source_state == \"file\":\n            source.write_bytes(b\"not a directory\")\n        events: list[ProgressEvent] = []\n        out = tmp_path / \"out.tar.gz\"\n        result = next(iter(TarArchive().run(\n            label=\"unwalkable\", source=str(source), out=str(out),\n            engine=\"python-tarfile\", progress=events.append,\n        )))\n        assert result.success is (source_state == \"missing\")\n        assert result.skipped is (source_state == \"missing\")\n        assert events == []\n        assert not out.exists()\n\n    def test_engine_selection_skip_can_end_after_scanning(self, tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n        source = tmp_path / \"src\"\n        source.mkdir()\n        (source / \"a-old\").write_bytes(b\"near miss\")\n        (source / \"b-old\").write_bytes(b\"another near miss\")\n        events: list[ProgressEvent] = []\n        out = tmp_path / \"out.tar.gz\"\n        result = next(iter(TarArchive().run(\n            label=\"empty\", source=str(source), out=str(out), items=[\"a\", \"b\"],\n            engine=\"python-tarfile\", progress=events.append,\n        )))\n        assert result.success is True\n        assert result.skipped is True\n        assert events == [ProgressEvent(\"empty\", \"scanning\", None, None)]\n        assert not out.exists()\n\n\nclass TestArchiveInputBytes:\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"sizes\", [[7, 19], [13, 31]])\n    def test_input_bytes_counts_regular_paths_and_hardlinks_but_not_directories_or_symlinks(\n        self, tmp_path: Path, sizes: list[int],\n    ) -> None:\n        source = tmp_path / \"src\"\n        source.mkdir()\n        first = source / \"a\"\n        second = source / \"a-old\"\n        first.write_bytes(b\"x\" * sizes[0])\n        second.write_bytes(b\"y\" * sizes[1])\n        hardlink = source / \"hardlink\"\n        os.link(first, hardlink)\n        directory = source / \"directory\"\n        directory.mkdir()\n        (directory / \"not-selected\").write_bytes(b\"must not recurse\")\n        symlink = source / \"symlink\"\n        symlink.symlink_to(second)\n        broken = source / \"broken\"\n        broken.symlink_to(source / \"absent\")\n        counts: list[int] = []\n        finalized: list[bool] = []\n        out = tmp_path / \"out.tar.gz\"\n        files = [first, directory, symlink, broken, second, hardlink]\n        _write_archive(out, source, files, on_bytes=counts.append, on_finalize=lambda: finalized.append(True))\n        assert counts == [sizes[0], sizes[0], sizes[0], sizes[0], sum(sizes), sum(sizes) + sizes[0]]\n        assert finalized == [True]\n        with tarfile.open(out) as archive:\n            members = {Path(member.name).name: member for member in archive.getmembers()}\n        assert set(members) == {path.name for path in files}\n        assert members[\"symlink\"].issym()\n        assert members[\"broken\"].issym()\n        assert members[\"directory\"].isdir()\n        assert members[\"hardlink\"].islnk()\n\n    def test_input_bytes_empty_writer_finalizes_without_member_callbacks(self, tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n        counts: list[int] = []\n        finalized: list[bool] = []\n        out = tmp_path / \"empty.tar.gz\"\n        _write_archive(out, tmp_path, [], on_bytes=counts.append, on_finalize=lambda: finalized.append(True))\n        assert counts == []\n        assert finalized == [True]\n        with tarfile.open(out) as archive:\n            assert archive.getmembers() == []\n\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"size\", [7, 29])\n    def test_input_bytes_failed_member_preserves_output_and_never_finalizes(\n        self, tmp_path: Path, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch, size: int,\n    ) -> None:\n        source = tmp_path / \"src\"\n        source.mkdir()\n        first = source / \"a\"\n        first.write_bytes(b\"x\" * size)\n        second = source / \"a-old\"\n        second.write_bytes(b\"not successfully added\")\n        out = tmp_path / \"out.tar.gz\"\n        out.write_bytes(b\"previous archive\")\n        counts: list[int] = []\n        finalized: list[bool] = []\n        original_add = tarfile.TarFile.add\n\n        def fail_second(archive: tarfile.TarFile, name: str, *args: object, **kwargs: object) -> None:\n            if Path(name) == second:\n                raise OSError(\"archive member failed\")\n            original_add(archive, name, *args, **kwargs)\n\n        monkeypatch.setattr(tarfile.TarFile, \"add\", fail_second)\n        with pytest.raises(OSError, match=\"archive member failed\"):\n            _write_archive(\n                out, source, [first, second], on_bytes=counts.append,\n                on_finalize=lambda: finalized.append(True),\n            )\n        assert counts == [size]\n        assert finalized == []\n        assert out.read_bytes() == b\"previous archive\"\n        assert sorted(path.name for path in tmp_path.iterdir()) == [\"out.tar.gz\", \"src\"]\n\n    def test_input_bytes_state_is_local_to_each_shared_capability_run(\n        self, tmp_path: Path, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\n    ) -> None:\n        capability = TarArchive()\n        monkeypatch.setattr(time, \"monotonic\", lambda: 42.0)\n        for label, size in [(\"a\", 7), (\"a-old\", 23)]:\n            source = tmp_path / label\n            source.mkdir()\n            (source / \"data\").write_bytes(b\"x\" * size)\n            events: list[ProgressEvent] = []\n            result = next(iter(capability.run(\n                label=label, source=str(source), out=str(tmp_path / f\"{label}.tar.gz\"),\n                engine=\"python-tarfile\", progress=events.append,\n            )))\n            assert result.success is True\n            assert events[-2:] == [\n                ProgressEvent(label, \"archiving\", size, size),\n                ProgressEvent(label, \"finalizing\", size, size),\n            ]\n\n\nclass TestProgressExceptionsSwallowed:\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"exception\", [ValueError(\"first\"), RuntimeError(\"first-old\")])\n    def test_ordinary_progress_exception_is_swallowed_after_delivering_exact_event(self, exception: Exception) -> None:\n        events = [ProgressEvent(\"a\", \"archiving\", 7, 31), ProgressEvent(\"a-old\", \"finalizing\", 19, 37)]\n        received: list[ProgressEvent] = []\n\n        def callback(event: ProgressEvent) -> None:\n            received.append(event)\n            raise exception\n\n        for event in events:\n            tar_archive._emit_progress(callback, event)\n        assert received == events\n        tar_archive._emit_progress(None, events[0])\n\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"exception\", [KeyboardInterrupt(), SystemExit(7), GeneratorExit(), BaseException(\"stop\")])\n    def test_base_exception_is_not_swallowed_by_progress_emitter(self, exception: BaseException) -> None:\n        event = ProgressEvent(\"interrupt\", \"scanning\", None, None)\n        received: list[ProgressEvent] = []\n\n        def callback(delivered: ProgressEvent) -> None:\n            received.append(delivered)\n            raise exception\n\n        with pytest.raises(type(exception)) as caught:\n            tar_archive._emit_progress(callback, event)\n        assert caught.value is exception\n        assert received == [event]\n\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"phase\", [\"scanning\", \"archiving\", \"finalizing\"])\n    def test_callback_exception_is_swallowed_and_real_engine_archive_finishes(self, tmp_path: Path, phase: str) -> None:\n        source = tmp_path / \"src\"\n        source.mkdir()\n        (source / \"a\").write_bytes(b\"first\")\n        (source / \"a-old\").write_bytes(b\"second payload\")\n        out = tmp_path / \"out.tar.gz\"\n        events: list[ProgressEvent] = []\n\n        def callback(event: ProgressEvent) -> None:\n            events.append(event)\n            if event.phase == phase:\n                raise RuntimeError(\"consumer unavailable\")\n\n        result = next(iter(TarArchive().run(\n            label=\"resilient\", source=str(source), out=str(out), engine=\"python-tarfile\", progress=callback,\n        )))\n        assert result.success is True\n        assert events[0] == ProgressEvent(\"resilient\", \"scanning\", None, None)\n        assert events[-1] == ProgressEvent(\"resilient\", \"finalizing\", 19, 19)\n        with tarfile.open(out) as archive:\n            assert {Path(member.name).name for member in archive.getmembers() if member.isfile()} == {\"a\", \"a-old\"}\n\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"exception\", [KeyboardInterrupt(), SystemExit(7)])\n    def test_engine_interrupt_is_not_swallowed_and_writer_cleans_temporary_archive(\n        self, tmp_path: Path, exception: BaseException,\n    ) -> None:\n        source = tmp_path / \"src\"\n        source.mkdir()\n        payload = source / \"a\"\n        payload.write_bytes(b\"first\")\n        out = tmp_path / \"out.tar.gz\"\n        out.write_bytes(b\"previous archive\")\n        cancel = threading.Event()\n        received: list[int] = []\n\n        def callback(done: int) -> None:\n            received.append(done)\n            cancel.set()\n            raise exception\n\n        with pytest.raises(type(exception)) as caught:\n            _write_archive(out, source, [payload], cancel=cancel, on_bytes=callback)\n        assert caught.value is exception\n        assert received == [5]\n        assert out.read_bytes() == b\"previous archive\"\n        assert sorted(path.name for path in tmp_path.iterdir()) == [\"out.tar.gz\", \"src\"]\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":2625}},"started_at_ms":1793566061539,"completed_at_ms":1793566061539}}
+{"timestamp":"2026-11-01T20:47:41.541Z","ordinal":25,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a198de-33e5-7523-a616-67a750116b57","call_id":"call_0179df1ee76a49a9ac957a6636f7d700","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"1cefc9\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000002625,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":6509,\"output\":\"FILE: /Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md\\n---\\nname: python-testing\\ndescription: Use when writing, fixing, or reviewing Python tests with pytest. Covers TDD, fixtures, mocking, parametrization, coverage. Triggers on \\\"pytest\\\", \\\"python test\\\", \\\"conftest\\\", \\\"pytest.mark\\\", \\\"parametrize\\\", \\\"pytest fixture\\\", \\\"python mock\\\".\\ncompatibility: \\\"Portable standalone compatibility copy of the strunk plugin skill for agents without that plugin; Claude Code uses the namespaced plugin skill.\\\"\\n---\\n\\n# Python Testing\\n\\nTDD: write the failing test (RED), make it pass (GREEN), refactor. One behavior per test. No logic in tests. Coverage target 80%, higher on critical paths.\\n\\n## Rulings\\n\\n**Mocking**\\n- Patch where the name is *used*, not where it's defined: `@patch(\\\"myapp.service.requests\\\")`, not `@patch(\\\"requests\\\")`.\\n- `autospec=True` so the mock rejects calls the real API would reject.\\n- Mock at the boundary (I/O, network, clock). Never mock the thing under test.\\n- Async: assert with `assert_awaited_once()`, not `assert_called_once()`.\\n\\n**Fixtures**\\n- `yield` for teardown; the line after `yield` is the cleanup.\\n- Default to function scope. Widen to `module`/`session` only for genuinely expensive resources.\\n- `autouse` hides dependencies — use sparingly; prefer explicit injection.\\n- `tmp_path` for temp files (auto-cleanup, `Path` API), not `tempfile`.\\n\\n**Parametrize**\\n- `@pytest.mark.parametrize` over loops — distinct test IDs, filterable with `-k`.\\n- Pass `ids=[...]` when params are objects or tuples; pytest already auto-names plain str/int/bool readably.\\n\\n**Config**\\n- One config in `pyproject.toml` (`[tool.pytest.ini_options]`), not a separate `pytest.ini`.\\n- `--strict-markers` so a typo'd marker fails instead of silently passing.\\n- Register custom markers — e.g. `slow`, `@pytest.mark.unit`, `@pytest.mark.integration` — so `--strict-markers` catches a typo.\\n- Coverage locally: `pytest --cov=src --cov-report=term-missing` — the missing-line report is the point; a bare percentage is not actionable.\\n\\n**Async (pytest-asyncio)**\\n- Default mode is `strict`: an async test with no `@pytest.mark.asyncio` is silently not collected. Set `asyncio_mode = \\\"auto\\\"` in `[tool.pytest.ini_options]` to drop the per-test marker.\\n- Use `@pytest_asyncio.fixture` for async fixtures in strict mode.\\n\\nFILE: /Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md\\n---\\nname: python-patterns\\ndescription: Use when writing, reviewing, or refactoring Python code. Covers idioms, naming, traps, toolchain, and security. Triggers on Python file edits, \\\"pythonic\\\", \\\"PEP 8\\\", \\\"python best practices\\\", \\\"python idioms\\\", \\\"bandit\\\".\\ncompatibility: \\\"Portable standalone compatibility copy of the strunk plugin skill for agents without that plugin; Claude Code uses the namespaced plugin skill.\\\"\\n---\\n\\n# Python Patterns\\n\\nPick a side. These are the rulings, not a tutorial.\\n\\n## Idioms that earn their place\\n\\n| Rule | Why |\\n|------|-----|\\n| `X \\\\| Y`, not `Union[X, Y]` | 3.10+ runtime syntax; clearer. On 3.9 it parses only under `from __future__ import annotations` and still breaks `get_type_hints`/`isinstance` — keep `Optional`/`Union` if you support 3.9. |\\n| `Protocol`, not `ABC`, for duck typing | Structural typing; no inheritance you don't control. |\\n| `@dataclass(frozen=True)` for immutable records, plain `dataclass` only when you must mutate, `NamedTuple` for lightweight immutable rows | Pydantic only when you need validation. |\\n| `raise New(...) from e` | Marks the explicit cause. A bare `raise New()` still chains implicitly (\\\"During handling...\\\"); use `from None` to suppress. |\\n| `@functools.wraps` on every decorator | Without it the wrapper loses `__name__`, `__doc__`, signature. |\\n| `pathlib.Path`, not `os.path` | One object, no string surgery. |\\n\\n## Naming (PEP 8)\\n\\n`snake_case` for modules, functions, variables. `CapWords` for classes. `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` for constants. Leading `_` for internal names.\\n\\n**Never name a `.py` file in kebab-case.** `my-script.py` is not importable (`import my-script` is a `SyntaxError`). Kebab-case belongs only in the `pyproject.toml` distribution name and the CLI command, both of which map to a `snake_case` module.\\n\\n## Traps\\n\\n```python\\n# Mutable default argument — shared across calls\\ndef bad(items=[]): ...\\ndef good(items=None):\\n    items = [] if items is None else items\\n\\n# Bare except — swallows SystemExit, KeyboardInterrupt\\ntry: ...\\nexcept Exception as e: ...        # name the exception\\n\\n# __slots__ kills __dict__ and dynamic attributes — use only on fixed,\\n# memory-sensitive classes you won't extend.\\n\\n# __double_leading is name-mangled to _Class__double_leading.\\n# Surprises you in subclasses, pickling, and monkey-patching.\\n\\nif value is None: ...             # never == None\\n```\\n\\nAvoid `from module import *`. Use `isinstance`, never `type(x) ==`.\\n\\n## Toolchain\\n\\n**black** to format, **isort** for imports, **ruff** to lint. Type annotations on every function signature — no exceptions for \\\"obvious\\\" returns.\\n\\n## Resources and laziness\\n\\nContext managers (`with`) for anything holding a resource. Generators for lazy iteration over anything you would otherwise materialize into a list.\\n\\n## Security\\n\\n- Read secrets with `os.environ[\\\"API_KEY\\\"]`, never `.get()` — a missing secret must raise `KeyError` at startup, not surface as `None` at request time.\\n- `python-dotenv` loads a local `.env` in development only. Never commit one.\\n- `bandit -r src/` for static security analysis.\\n\\nFILE: tests/tools/backup/test_progress.py\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport os\\nimport tarfile\\nimport threading\\nimport time\\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\nfrom typing import Literal, get_type_hints\\n\\nimport pytest\\n\\nfrom backup.capabilities import tar_archive\\nfrom backup.capabilities.tar_archive import TarArchive, _write_archive\\nfrom backup.step_result import ProgressEvent\\n\\n\\nclass TestProgressEventRecord:\\n    def test_event_record_has_exact_named_tuple_fields_types_and_no_defaults(self) -> None:\\n        assert ProgressEvent.__bases__ == (tuple,)\\n        assert ProgressEvent._fields == (\\\"label\\\", \\\"phase\\\", \\\"done_bytes\\\", \\\"total_bytes\\\")\\n        assert ProgressEvent._field_defaults == {}\\n        assert get_type_hints(ProgressEvent) == {\\n            \\\"label\\\": str,\\n            \\\"phase\\\": Literal[\\\"scanning\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", \\\"finalizing\\\"],\\n            \\\"done_bytes\\\": int | None,\\n            \\\"total_bytes\\\": int | None,\\n        }\\n\\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\\n        \\\"label,phase,done_bytes,total_bytes\\\",\\n        [\\n            (\\\"documents\\\", \\\"scanning\\\", None, None),\\n            (\\\"documents-old\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", 37, 101),\\n            (\\\"\\\", \\\"finalizing\\\", 0, 0),\\n            (\\\"photos\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", 2**40, 2**41),\\n            (\\\"photos\\\", \\\"scanning\\\", 0, None),\\n            (\\\"documents\\\", \\\"finalizing\\\", None, 101),\\n            (\\\"Příliš žluťoučký 🗃️\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", 2**63, 2**80),\\n        ],\\n    )\\n    def test_event_record_preserves_each_positional_field_and_byte_value(\\n        self,\\n        label: str,\\n        phase: Literal[\\\"scanning\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", \\\"finalizing\\\"],\\n        done_bytes: int | None,\\n        total_bytes: int | None,\\n    ) -> None:\\n        event = ProgressEvent(label, phase, done_bytes, total_bytes)\\n        assert event.label == label\\n        assert event.phase == phase\\n        assert event.done_bytes == done_bytes\\n        assert event.total_bytes == total_bytes\\n        assert event[0] == event.label\\n        assert event[1] == event.phase\\n        assert event[2] == event.done_bytes\\n        assert event[3] == event.total_bytes\\n        assert tuple(event) == (label, phase, done_bytes, total_bytes)\\n        assert event == ProgressEvent(\\n            total_bytes=total_bytes,\\n            done_bytes=done_bytes,\\n            phase=phase,\\n            label=label,\\n        )\\n        assert event == ProgressEvent(label, phase=phase, done_bytes=done_bytes, total_bytes=total_bytes)\\n\\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\\\"field\\\", [\\\"label\\\", \\\"phase\\\", \\\"done_bytes\\\", \\\"total_bytes\\\"])\\n    def test_event_record_rejects_field_mutation(self, field: str) -> None:\\n        event = ProgressEvent(\\\"documents\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", 37, 101)\\n        assert not hasattr(event, \\\"__dict__\\\")\\n        with pytest.raises(AttributeError):\\n            setattr(event, field, None)\\n        assert tuple(event) == (\\\"documents\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", 37, 101)\\n\\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\\n        \\\"args\\\",\\n        [(), (\\\"documents\\\",), (\\\"documents\\\", \\\"scanning\\\"), (\\\"documents\\\", \\\"scanning\\\", None)],\\n    )\\n    def test_event_record_requires_all_four_arguments(self, args: tuple[object, ...]) -> None:\\n        with pytest.raises(TypeError):\\n            ProgressEvent(*args)\\n\\n    def test_event_record_distinguishes_similar_labels_and_each_field(self) -> None:\\n        event = ProgressEvent(\\\"documents\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", 37, 101)\\n        assert event != ProgressEvent(\\\"documents-old\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", 37, 101)\\n        assert event != ProgressEvent(\\\"documents\\\", \\\"finalizing\\\", 37, 101)\\n        assert event != ProgressEvent(\\\"documents\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", 38, 101)\\n        assert event != ProgressEvent(\\\"documents\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", 37, 102)\\n\\n    def test_event_record_crosses_worker_thread_without_sharing_mutable_call_state(self) -> None:\\n        original = ProgressEvent(\\\"documents\\\", \\\"scanning\\\", None, None)\\n\\n        def update_in_worker(event: ProgressEvent) -> tuple[ProgressEvent, ProgressEvent]:\\n            updated = event._replace(phase=\\\"archiving\\\", done_bytes=37, total_bytes=101)\\n            other = ProgressEvent(\\\"photos\\\", \\\"finalizing\\\", 0, 0)\\n            return updated, other\\n\\n        with ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=1) as executor:\\n            updated, other = executor.submit(update_in_worker, original).result(timeout=5)\\n        assert tuple(original) == (\\\"documents\\\", \\\"scanning\\\", None, None)\\n        assert (original.label, original.phase, original.done_bytes, original.total_bytes) == (\\n            \\\"documents\\\",\\n            \\\"scanning\\\",\\n            None,\\n            None,\\n        )\\n        assert (other.label, other.phase, other.done_bytes, other.total_bytes) == (\\\"photos\\\", \\\"finalizing\\\", 0, 0)\\n        assert isinstance(updated, ProgressEvent)\\n        assert tuple(updated) == (\\\"documents\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", 37, 101)\\n        replacements = [\\n            (original._replace(label=\\\"photos\\\"), (\\\"photos\\\", \\\"scanning\\\", None, None)),\\n            (original._replace(phase=\\\"finalizing\\\"), (\\\"documents\\\", \\\"finalizing\\\", None, None)),\\n            (original._replace(done_bytes=37), (\\\"documents\\\", \\\"scanning\\\", 37, None)),\\n            (original._replace(total_bytes=101), (\\\"documents\\\", \\\"scanning\\\", None, 101)),\\n            (updated._replace(done_bytes=None), (\\\"documents\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", None, 101)),\\n            (updated._replace(total_bytes=None), (\\\"documents\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", 37, None)),\\n        ]\\n        for replacement, expected in replacements:\\n            assert isinstance(replacement, ProgressEvent)\\n            assert (\\n                replacement.label,\\n                replacement.phase,\\n                replacement.done_bytes,\\n                replacement.total_bytes,\\n            ) == expected\\n            assert tuple(replacement) == expected\\n\\n\\nclass TestArchiveEngineProgress:\\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\\\"engine\\\", [\\\"python-tarfile\\\", \\\"system-tar\\\"])\\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\\\"label,sizes\\\", [(\\\"docs\\\", [7, 19]), (\\\"docs-old\\\", [11, 31])])\\n    def test_engine_reports_ordered_phases_and_selected_input_bytes_before_publication(\\n        self, tmp_path: Path, engine: str, label: str, sizes: list[int],\\n    ) -> None:\\n        source = tmp_path / \\\"src\\\"\\n        source.mkdir()\\n        for name, size in zip([\\\"a-old\\\", \\\"b\\\"], sizes, strict=True):\\n            (source / name).write_bytes(b\\\"x\\\" * size)\\n        (source / \\\"a\\\").write_bytes(b\\\"excluded\\\" * 13)\\n        out = tmp_path / \\\"out.tar.gz\\\"\\n        out.write_bytes(b\\\"previous archive\\\")\\n        events: list[ProgressEvent] = []\\n        finalizing_output: list[bytes] = []\\n\\n        def progress(event: ProgressEvent) -> None:\\n            events.append(event)\\n            if event.phase == \\\"finalizing\\\":\\n                finalizing_output.append(out.read_bytes())\\n\\n        result = next(iter(TarArchive().run(\\n            label=label, source=str(source), out=str(out), engine=engine,\\n            items=[\\\"a\\\", \\\"a-old\\\", \\\"b\\\"], excludes=[\\\"a\\\"], progress=progress,\\n        )))\\n        assert result.success is True\\n        assert finalizing_output == [b\\\"previous archive\\\"]\\n        total = sum(sizes)\\n        done = total if engine == \\\"python-tarfile\\\" else None\\n        assert events[0] == ProgressEvent(label, \\\"scanning\\\", None, None)\\n        assert events[1] == ProgressEvent(label, \\\"archiving\\\", 0 if done is not None else None, total)\\n        assert events[-1] == ProgressEvent(label, \\\"finalizing\\\", done, total)\\n        assert all(event.label == label for event in events)\\n        assert all(event.total_bytes == total for event in events[1:])\\n        assert all(event.phase == \\\"archiving\\\" for event in events[1:-1])\\n        if engine == \\\"system-tar\\\":\\n            assert all(event.done_bytes is None for event in events)\\n        else:\\n            assert events[-2] == ProgressEvent(label, \\\"archiving\\\", total, total)\\n        with tarfile.open(out) as archive:\\n            assert {Path(member.name).name for member in archive.getmembers() if member.isfile()} == {\\\"a-old\\\", \\\"b\\\"}\\n        assert out.stat().st_mode & 0o777 == 0o600\\n\\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\\\"sizes\\\", [[3, 7, 11, 17], [5, 13, 19, 23]])\\n    def test_engine_throttles_at_two_tenths_and_flushes_short_final_count(\\n        self, tmp_path: Path, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch, sizes: list[int],\\n    ) -> None:\\n        source = tmp_path / \\\"src\\\"\\n        source.mkdir()\\n        names = [\\\"a\\\", \\\"b\\\", \\\"c\\\", \\\"d\\\"]\\n        for name, size in zip(names, sizes, strict=True):\\n            (source / name).write_bytes(b\\\"x\\\" * size)\\n        clock = [0.0]\\n        moments = dict(zip(names, [0.199, 0.2, 0.399, 0.3999], strict=True))\\n        original_add = tarfile.TarFile.add\\n\\n        def add_with_clock(archive: tarfile.TarFile, name: str, *args: object, **kwargs: object) -> None:\\n            original_add(archive, name, *args, **kwargs)\\n            clock[0] = moments[Path(name).name]\\n\\n        monkeypatch.setattr(time, \\\"monotonic\\\", lambda: clock[0])\\n        monkeypatch.setattr(tarfile.TarFile, \\\"add\\\", add_with_clock)\\n        events: list[ProgressEvent] = []\\n        result = next(iter(TarArchive().run(\\n            label=\\\"timed\\\", source=str(source), out=str(tmp_path / \\\"timed.tar.gz\\\"),\\n            engine=\\\"python-tarfile\\\", items=names, progress=events.append,\\n        )))\\n        assert result.success is True\\n        total = sum(sizes)\\n        assert events == [\\n            ProgressEvent(\\\"timed\\\", \\\"scanning\\\", None, None),\\n            ProgressEvent(\\\"timed\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", 0, total),\\n            ProgressEvent(\\\"timed\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", sum(sizes[:2]), total),\\n            ProgressEvent(\\\"timed\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", total, total),\\n            ProgressEvent(\\\"timed\\\", \\\"finalizing\\\", total, total),\\n        ]\\n\\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\\\"label,size\\\", [(\\\"first\\\", 7), (\\\"first-old\\\", 29)])\\n    def test_engine_short_archive_flushes_without_waiting_or_duplicate_final_count(\\n        self, tmp_path: Path, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch, label: str, size: int,\\n    ) -> None:\\n        source = tmp_path / \\\"src\\\"\\n        source.mkdir()\\n        (source / \\\"payload\\\").write_bytes(b\\\"x\\\" * size)\\n        monkeypatch.setattr(time, \\\"monotonic\\\", lambda: 42.0)\\n        events: list[ProgressEvent] = []\\n        result = next(iter(TarArchive().run(\\n            label=label, source=str(source), out=str(tmp_path / \\\"out.tar.gz\\\"),\\n            engine=\\\"python-tarfile\\\", progress=events.append,\\n        )))\\n        assert result.success is True\\n        assert events == [\\n            ProgressEvent(label, \\\"scanning\\\", None, None),\\n            ProgressEvent(label, \\\"archiving\\\", 0, size),\\n            ProgressEvent(label, \\\"archiving\\\", size, size),\\n            ProgressEvent(label, \\\"finalizing\\\", size, size),\\n        ]\\n\\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\\\"engine\\\", [\\\"python-tarfile\\\", \\\"system-tar\\\"])\\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\\\"items\\\", [None, [\\\"a\\\", \\\"b\\\"]])\\n    def test_engine_direct_dry_run_never_calls_progress(\\n        self, tmp_path: Path, engine: str, items: list[str] | None,\\n    ) -> None:\\n        source = tmp_path / \\\"src\\\"\\n        source.mkdir()\\n        (source / \\\"a\\\").write_bytes(b\\\"first\\\")\\n        (source / \\\"b\\\").write_bytes(b\\\"second payload\\\")\\n        out = tmp_path / \\\"out.tar.gz\\\"\\n        events: list[ProgressEvent] = []\\n        result = next(iter(TarArchive().run(\\n            label=\\\"preview\\\", source=str(source), out=str(out), engine=engine,\\n            items=items, dry_run=True, progress=events.append,\\n        )))\\n        assert result.success is True\\n        assert events == []\\n        assert not out.exists()\\n\\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\\\"source_state\\\", [\\\"missing\\\", \\\"file\\\"])\\n    def test_engine_unwalkable_source_emits_no_fabricated_activity(\\n        self, tmp_path: Path, source_state: str,\\n    ) -> None:\\n        source = tmp_path / source_state\\n        if source_state == \\\"file\\\":\\n            source.write_bytes(b\\\"not a directory\\\")\\n        events: list[ProgressEvent] = []\\n        out = tmp_path / \\\"out.tar.gz\\\"\\n        result = next(iter(TarArchive().run(\\n            label=\\\"unwalkable\\\", source=str(source), out=str(out),\\n            engine=\\\"python-tarfile\\\", progress=events.append,\\n        )))\\n        assert result.success is (source_state == \\\"missing\\\")\\n        assert result.skipped is (source_state == \\\"missing\\\")\\n        assert events == []\\n        assert not out.exists()\\n\\n    def test_engine_selection_skip_can_end_after_scanning(self, tmp_path: Path) -> None:\\n        source = tmp_path / \\\"src\\\"\\n        source.mkdir()\\n        (source / \\\"a-old\\\").write_bytes(b\\\"near miss\\\")\\n        (source / \\\"b-old\\\").write_bytes(b\\\"another near miss\\\")\\n        events: list[ProgressEvent] = []\\n        out = tmp_path / \\\"out.tar.gz\\\"\\n        result = next(iter(TarArchive().run(\\n            label=\\\"empty\\\", source=str(source), out=str(out), items=[\\\"a\\\", \\\"b\\\"],\\n            engine=\\\"python-tarfile\\\", progress=events.append,\\n        )))\\n        assert result.success is True\\n        assert result.skipped is True\\n        assert events == [ProgressEvent(\\\"empty\\\", \\\"scanning\\\", None, None)]\\n        assert not out.exists()\\n\\n\\nclass TestArchiveInputBytes:\\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\\\"sizes\\\", [[7, 19], [13, 31]])\\n    def test_input_bytes_counts_regular_paths_and_hardlinks_but_not_directories_or_symlinks(\\n        self, tmp_path: Path, sizes: list[int],\\n    ) -> None:\\n        source = tmp_path / \\\"src\\\"\\n        source.mkdir()\\n        first = source / \\\"a\\\"\\n        second = source / \\\"a-old\\\"\\n        first.write_bytes(b\\\"x\\\" * sizes[0])\\n        second.write_bytes(b\\\"y\\\" * sizes[1])\\n        hardlink = source / \\\"hardlink\\\"\\n        os.link(first, hardlink)\\n        directory = source / \\\"directory\\\"\\n        directory.mkdir()\\n        (directory / \\\"not-selected\\\").write_bytes(b\\\"must not recurse\\\")\\n        symlink = source / \\\"symlink\\\"\\n        symlink.symlink_to(second)\\n        broken = source / \\\"broken\\\"\\n        broken.symlink_to(source / \\\"absent\\\")\\n        counts: list[int] = []\\n        finalized: list[bool] = []\\n        out = tmp_path / \\\"out.tar.gz\\\"\\n        files = [first, directory, symlink, broken, second, hardlink]\\n        _write_archive(out, source, files, on_bytes=counts.append, on_finalize=lambda: finalized.append(True))\\n        assert counts == [sizes[0], sizes[0], sizes[0], sizes[0], sum(sizes), sum(sizes) + sizes[0]]\\n        assert finalized == [True]\\n        with tarfile.open(out) as archive:\\n            members = {Path(member.name).name: member for member in archive.getmembers()}\\n        assert set(members) == {path.name for path in files}\\n        assert members[\\\"symlink\\\"].issym()\\n        assert members[\\\"broken\\\"].issym()\\n        assert members[\\\"directory\\\"].isdir()\\n        assert members[\\\"hardlink\\\"].islnk()\\n\\n    def test_input_bytes_empty_writer_finalizes_without_member_callbacks(self, tmp_path: Path) -> None:\\n        counts: list[int] = []\\n        finalized: list[bool] = []\\n        out = tmp_path / \\\"empty.tar.gz\\\"\\n        _write_archive(out, tmp_path, [], on_bytes=counts.append, on_finalize=lambda: finalized.append(True))\\n        assert counts == []\\n        assert finalized == [True]\\n        with tarfile.open(out) as archive:\\n            assert archive.getmembers() == []\\n\\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\\\"size\\\", [7, 29])\\n    def test_input_bytes_failed_member_preserves_output_and_never_finalizes(\\n        self, tmp_path: Path, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch, size: int,\\n    ) -> None:\\n        source = tmp_path / \\\"src\\\"\\n        source.mkdir()\\n        first = source / \\\"a\\\"\\n        first.write_bytes(b\\\"x\\\" * size)\\n        second = source / \\\"a-old\\\"\\n        second.write_bytes(b\\\"not successfully added\\\")\\n        out = tmp_path / \\\"out.tar.gz\\\"\\n        out.write_bytes(b\\\"previous archive\\\")\\n        counts: list[int] = []\\n        finalized: list[bool] = []\\n        original_add = tarfile.TarFile.add\\n\\n        def fail_second(archive: tarfile.TarFile, name: str, *args: object, **kwargs: object) -> None:\\n            if Path(name) == second:\\n                raise OSError(\\\"archive member failed\\\")\\n            original_add(archive, name, *args, **kwargs)\\n\\n        monkeypatch.setattr(tarfile.TarFile, \\\"add\\\", fail_second)\\n        with pytest.raises(OSError, match=\\\"archive member failed\\\"):\\n            _write_archive(\\n                out, source, [first, second], on_bytes=counts.append,\\n                on_finalize=lambda: finalized.append(True),\\n            )\\n        assert counts == [size]\\n        assert finalized == []\\n        assert out.read_bytes() == b\\\"previous archive\\\"\\n        assert sorted(path.name for path in tmp_path.iterdir()) == [\\\"out.tar.gz\\\", \\\"src\\\"]\\n\\n    def test_input_bytes_state_is_local_to_each_shared_capability_run(\\n        self, tmp_path: Path, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\\n    ) -> None:\\n        capability = TarArchive()\\n        monkeypatch.setattr(time, \\\"monotonic\\\", lambda: 42.0)\\n        for label, size in [(\\\"a\\\", 7), (\\\"a-old\\\", 23)]:\\n            source = tmp_path / label\\n            source.mkdir()\\n            (source / \\\"data\\\").write_bytes(b\\\"x\\\" * size)\\n            events: list[ProgressEvent] = []\\n            result = next(iter(capability.run(\\n                label=label, source=str(source), out=str(tmp_path / f\\\"{label}.tar.gz\\\"),\\n                engine=\\\"python-tarfile\\\", progress=events.append,\\n            )))\\n            assert result.success is True\\n            assert events[-2:] == [\\n                ProgressEvent(label, \\\"archiving\\\", size, size),\\n                ProgressEvent(label, \\\"finalizing\\\", size, size),\\n            ]\\n\\n\\nclass TestProgressExceptionsSwallowed:\\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\\\"exception\\\", [ValueError(\\\"first\\\"), RuntimeError(\\\"first-old\\\")])\\n    def test_ordinary_progress_exception_is_swallowed_after_delivering_exact_event(self, exception: Exception) -> None:\\n        events = [ProgressEvent(\\\"a\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", 7, 31), ProgressEvent(\\\"a-old\\\", \\\"finalizing\\\", 19, 37)]\\n        received: list[ProgressEvent] = []\\n\\n        def callback(event: ProgressEvent) -> None:\\n            received.append(event)\\n            raise exception\\n\\n        for event in events:\\n            tar_archive._emit_progress(callback, event)\\n        assert received == events\\n        tar_archive._emit_progress(None, events[0])\\n\\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\\\"exception\\\", [KeyboardInterrupt(), SystemExit(7), GeneratorExit(), BaseException(\\\"stop\\\")])\\n    def test_base_exception_is_not_swallowed_by_progress_emitter(self, exception: BaseException) -> None:\\n        event = ProgressEvent(\\\"interrupt\\\", \\\"scanning\\\", None, None)\\n        received: list[ProgressEvent] = []\\n\\n        def callback(delivered: ProgressEvent) -> None:\\n            received.append(delivered)\\n            raise exception\\n\\n        with pytest.raises(type(exception)) as caught:\\n            tar_archive._emit_progress(callback, event)\\n        assert caught.value is exception\\n        assert received == [event]\\n\\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\\\"phase\\\", [\\\"scanning\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", \\\"finalizing\\\"])\\n    def test_callback_exception_is_swallowed_and_real_engine_archive_finishes(self, tmp_path: Path, phase: str) -> None:\\n        source = tmp_path / \\\"src\\\"\\n        source.mkdir()\\n        (source / \\\"a\\\").write_bytes(b\\\"first\\\")\\n        (source / \\\"a-old\\\").write_bytes(b\\\"second payload\\\")\\n        out = tmp_path / \\\"out.tar.gz\\\"\\n        events: list[ProgressEvent] = []\\n\\n        def callback(event: ProgressEvent) -> None:\\n            events.append(event)\\n            if event.phase == phase:\\n                raise RuntimeError(\\\"consumer unavailable\\\")\\n\\n        result = next(iter(TarArchive().run(\\n            label=\\\"resilient\\\", source=str(source), out=str(out), engine=\\\"python-tarfile\\\", progress=callback,\\n        )))\\n        assert result.success is True\\n        assert events[0] == ProgressEvent(\\\"resilient\\\", \\\"scanning\\\", None, None)\\n        assert events[-1] == ProgressEvent(\\\"resilient\\\", \\\"finalizing\\\", 19, 19)\\n       