+{"timestamp":"2026-11-01T21:25:24.798Z","ordinal":15,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a19900-af79-7123-bbfd-55dabe96090b","turn_id":"01a19900-af9f-7d60-ae69-d05d6ac761a7","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-543ce944-75de-4b14-8410-186effc7d67a","process_id":"94125","command":["/opt/homebrew/bin/bash","-lc","cat docs/dev/tmp/dispatch-ivan-3-retry-1.txt"],"cwd":"file:///Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/gems","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat docs/dev/tmp/dispatch-ivan-3-retry-1.txt","name":"dispatch-ivan-3-retry-1.txt","path":"docs/dev/tmp/dispatch-ivan-3-retry-1.txt"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"\nYou are Ivan, the implementor. Make all failing tests pass. Tests ARE the\nspec. Do NOT modify test files unless your allowlist below names them (a\ntest-only task lists them on purpose). Do NOT read the task's acceptance criteria —\nnone are provided to you on purpose.\n\n## Failing tests\n\n/Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/gems/tests/tools/backup/progress_runner_cases.py\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport queue\nimport threading\nfrom collections.abc import Callable, Iterator\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nfrom contextlib import closing\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom typing import Any\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom backup.capabilities import CAPABILITIES\nfrom backup.config import BackupConfig, BackupInstance\nfrom backup.runner import Runner\nfrom backup.step_result import PlanEntry, ProgressEvent, StepResult\n\n\ndef _frames(label: str, value: int = 7) -> list[ProgressEvent]:\n    return [\n        ProgressEvent(label, \"scanning\", None, None),\n        ProgressEvent(label, \"archiving\", value, value + 31),\n        ProgressEvent(label, \"finalizing\", value + 31, value + 31),\n    ]\n\n\nclass _Capability:\n    inputs: dict[str, object] = {}\n\n    def __init__(self, produce: Callable[[dict[str, Any]], Iterator[StepResult]]) -> None:\n        self.produce = produce\n        self.calls: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n        self.plans: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n\n    def plan(self, **kwargs: Any) -> PlanEntry:\n        self.plans.append(kwargs)\n        label = kwargs[\"label\"]\n        return PlanEntry(label, f\"/source/{label}\", f\"/archives/{label}.tar.gz\", \"run\", \"\", False)\n\n    def run(self, **kwargs: Any) -> Iterator[StepResult]:\n        self.calls.append(kwargs)\n        yield from self.produce(kwargs)\n\n\ndef _config(monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch, capability: _Capability, labels: tuple[str, ...]) -> BackupConfig:\n    monkeypatch.setitem(CAPABILITIES, \"controlled-progress\", capability)\n    return BackupConfig(\n        instances={label: BackupInstance(use=\"controlled-progress\", order=index) for index, label in enumerate(labels)},\n        excludes=(\"cache\", \"cache-old\"),\n    )\n\n\ndef _outcomes(results: Iterator[StepResult] | list[StepResult]) -> list[tuple[str, bool, str]]:\n    return [(result.label, result.success, result.message) for result in results]\n\n\ndef _blocking_waits(monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch) -> list[tuple[int, float | None]]:\n    waits: list[tuple[int, float | None]] = []\n    original_get = queue.Queue.get\n\n    def get(instance: queue.Queue[Any], block: bool = True, timeout: float | None = None) -> Any:\n        if block:\n            waits.append((threading.get_ident(), timeout))\n        return original_get(instance, block=block, timeout=timeout)\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(queue.Queue, \"get\", get)\n    return waits\n\n\nclass _OrderedCapability(_Capability):\n    def __init__(self, success: bool) -> None:\n        super().__init__(self.produce_ordered)\n        self.success = success\n        self.emitted: list[ProgressEvent] = []\n        self.worker_threads: list[int] = []\n        self.old_done = threading.Event()\n\n    def produce_ordered(self, kwargs: dict[str, Any]) -> Iterator[StepResult]:\n        self.worker_threads.append(threading.get_ident())\n        label = kwargs[\"label\"]\n        if label == \"vault\":\n            assert self.old_done.wait(3), \"second label was not submitted concurrently\"\n        for event in _frames(label, 7 if label == \"vault\" else 19):\n            self.emitted.append(event)\n            kwargs[\"progress\"](event)\n        if label == \"vault-old\":\n            self.old_done.set()\n        yield StepResult(label, self.success, f\"{label}: {'stored' if self.success else 'failed'}\")\n\n\nclass TestRunnerCallingThread:\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"jobs\", [1, 3])\n    def test_runner_honors_requested_worker_concurrency(self, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch, jobs: int) -> None:\n        started = {label: threading.Event() for label in (\"one\", \"two\", \"three\")}\n        release = threading.Event()\n        idle = threading.Event()\n\n        def produce(kwargs: dict[str, Any]) -> Iterator[StepResult]:\n            started[kwargs[\"label\"]].set()\n            assert release.wait(3), \"consumer did not release workers\"\n            yield StepResult(kwargs[\"label\"], True, \"stored\")\n\n        capability = _Capability(produce)\n        cfg = _config(monkeypatch, capability, tuple(started))\n        runner = Runner(cfg, jobs=jobs, on_tick=idle.set)\n        with ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=1) as executor:\n            future = executor.submit(lambda: list(runner.run(list(cfg.instances.items()))))\n            try:\n                if jobs == 1:\n                    assert idle.wait(2), \"runner did not enter an idle wait\"\n                    assert sum(event.is_set() for event in started.values()) == 1\n                else:\n                    assert all(event.wait(2) for event in started.values()), \"requested workers did not all start\"\n            finally:\n                release.set()\n            results = future.result(timeout=5)\n        assert sorted(_outcomes(results)) == [(label, True, \"stored\") for label in sorted(started)]\n        assert all(event.is_set() for event in started.values())\n\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\n        \"inherit,remove,add,expected\",\n        [\n            (True, (\"cache\",), (\"extra\", \"cache-old\"), [\"cache-old\", \"extra\"]),\n            (False, (), (\"private\",), [\"private\"]),\n        ],\n    )\n    def test_runner_forwards_inputs_effective_exclusions_and_one_runtime_timestamp(\n        self,\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\n        inherit: bool,\n        remove: tuple[str, ...],\n        add: tuple[str, ...],\n        expected: list[str],\n    ) -> None:\n        capability = _Capability(lambda kwargs: iter([StepResult(kwargs[\"label\"], True, \"stored\")]))\n        cfg = _config(monkeypatch, capability, (\"docs\", \"photos\"))\n        cfg = BackupConfig(\n            excludes=cfg.excludes,\n            instances={\n                label: BackupInstance(\n                    use=\"controlled-progress\",\n                    with_={\"source\": f\"/unique/{label}\", \"items\": [label, f\"{label}-old\"]},\n                    inherit_excludes=inherit,\n                    exclude_remove=remove,\n                    exclude_add=add,\n                )\n                for label in cfg.instances\n            },\n        )\n        before = datetime.now()\n        results = list(Runner(cfg, jobs=2).run(list(cfg.instances.items())))\n        after = datetime.now()\n        assert sorted(_outcomes(results)) == [(label, True, \"stored\") for label in sorted(cfg.instances)]\n        assert len(capability.calls) == 2\n        for call in capability.calls:\n            label = call[\"label\"]\n            assert call[\"source\"] == f\"/unique/{label}\"\n            assert call[\"items\"] == [label, f\"{label}-old\"]\n            assert call[\"excludes\"] == expected\n            assert isinstance(call[\"now\"], datetime)\n            assert before <= call[\"now\"] <= after\n        assert capability.calls[0][\"now\"] == capability.calls[1][\"now\"]\n\n    def test_runner_preserves_every_result_from_each_capability(self, monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch) -> None:\n        received: list[ProgressEvent] = []\n\n        def produce(kwargs: dict[str, Any]) -> Iterator[StepResult]:\n            for index, (success, message, skipped) in enumerate(\n                [(True, \"first stored\", False), (False, \"second failed\", False), (True, \"third skipped\", True)]\n            ):\n                kwargs[\"progress\"](ProgressEvent(kwargs[\"label\"], \"archiving\", index, 3))\n                yield StepResult(kwargs[\"label\"], success, message, skipped=skipped)\n\n        capability = _Capability(produce)\n        cfg = _config(monkeypatch, capability, (\"docs\",))\n        rows = []\n        for result in Runner(cfg, on_progress=received.append).run(list(cfg.instances.items())):\n            assert received == [ProgressEvent(\"docs\", \"archiving\", index, 3) for index in range(3)]\n            rows.append((result.label, result.success, result.message, result.archive, result.skipped))\n        assert rows == [\n            (\"docs\", True, \"first stored\", None, False),\n            (\"docs\", False, \"second failed\", None, False),\n            (\"docs\", True, \"third skipped\", None, True),\n        ]\n\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"background_consumer\", [False, True])\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"success\", [False, True])\n    def test_runner_preserves_fifo_events_and_drains_before_results_on_calling_thread(\n        self,\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\n        background_consumer: bool,\n        success: bool,\n    ) -> None:\n        received: list[ProgressEvent] = []\n        observer_threads: list[int] = []\n\n        def observe(event: ProgressEvent) -> None:\n            observer_threads.append(threading.get_ident())\n            received.append(event)\n\n        capability = _OrderedCapability(success)\n        cfg = _config(monkeypatch, capability, (\"vault\", \"vault-old\"))\n        runner = Runner(cfg, jobs=2, on_progress=observe)\n\n        def consume() -> tuple[int, list[StepResult]]:\n            results = []\n            for result in runner.run(list(cfg.instances.items())):\n                expected = _frames(result.label, 7 if result.label == \"vault\" else 19)\n                assert [event for event in received if event.label == result.label] == expected\n                results.append(result)\n            return threading.get_ident(), results\n\n        with ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=1) as executor:\n            caller, results = executor.submit(consume).result(timeout=5) if background_consumer else consume()\n        assert received == capability.emitted == _frames(\"vault-old\", 19) + _frames(\"vault\", 7)\n        assert observer_threads == [caller] * 6\n        assert all(worker != caller for worker in capability.worker_threads)\n        assert {result.label: (result.success, result.message) for result in results} == {\n            label: (success, f\"{label}: {'stored' if success else 'failed'}\") for label in (\"vault\", \"vault-old\")\n        }\n        for call in capability.calls:\n            assert call[\"progress\"] is not observe\n            assert call[\"excludes\"] == [\"cache\", \"cache-old\"]\n            assert not {\"on_progress\", \"on_tick\", \"console\"}.intersection(call)\n\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"with_observer\", [False, True])\n    def test_runner_ticks_without_events_and_isolates_each_observer_exception(\n        self,\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\n        with_observer: bool,\n    ) -> None:\n        release = threading.Event()\n        events: list[ProgressEvent] = []\n        ticks: list[int] = []\n        waits = _blocking_waits(monkeypatch)\n\n        def produce(kwargs: dict[str, Any]) -> Iterator[StepResult]:\n            assert release.wait(3), \"idle runner did not offer ticks\"\n            if kwargs[\"progress\"] is not None:\n                for event in _frames(kwargs[\"label\"], 23):\n                    kwargs[\"progress\"](event)\n            yield StepResult(kwargs[\"label\"], True, \"writer unaffected\")\n\n        def tick() -> None:\n            ticks.append(threading.get_ident())\n            if len(ticks) == 3:\n                release.set()\n            raise ValueError(\"broken elapsed observer\")\n\n        def observe(event: ProgressEvent) -> None:\n            events.append(event)\n            raise RuntimeError(\"broken progress observer\")\n\n        capability = _Capability(produce)\n        cfg = _config(monkeypatch, capability, (\"quiet\",))\n        runner = Runner(\n            cfg,\n            on_progress=observe if with_observer else None,\n            on_tick=tick,\n        )\n        try:\n            with ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=1) as executor:\n                caller, results = executor.submit(\n                    lambda: (threading.get_ident(), list(runner.run(list(cfg.instances.items()))))\n                ).result(timeout=5)\n        finally:\n            release.set()\n        assert _outcomes(results) == [(\"quiet\", True, \"writer unaffected\")]\n        assert events == (_frames(\"quiet\", 23) if with_observer else [])\n        assert len(ticks) >= 3\n        assert set(ticks) == {caller}\n        caller_waits = [timeout for thread, timeout in waits if thread == caller]\n        assert len(caller_waits) >= 3\n        assert all(timeout == 0.2 for timeout in caller_waits)\n\n\nclass TestRunnerSuppression:\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"dry_run,with_observer\", [(True, True), (False, False)])\n    def test_runner_passes_no_progress_for_dry_run_or_absent_observer(\n        self,\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\n        dry_run: bool,\n        with_observer: bool,\n    ) -> None:\n        observed: list[ProgressEvent] = []\n        ticks: list[int] = []\n\n        def produce(kwargs: dict[str, Any]) -> Iterator[StepResult]:\n            if dry_run:\n                threading.Event().wait(0.45)\n            yield StepResult(kwargs[\"label\"], True, \"preview\" if dry_run else \"stored\")\n\n        capability = _Capability(produce)\n        cfg = _config(monkeypatch, capability, (\"docs\", \"docs-old\"))\n        runner = Runner(\n            cfg,\n            dry_run=dry_run,\n            on_progress=observed.append if with_observer else None,\n            on_tick=lambda: ticks.append(1),\n        )\n        assert {result.label for result in runner.run(list(cfg.instances.items()))} == {\"docs\", \"docs-old\"}\n        assert len(capability.calls) == 2\n        assert all(call[\"progress\"] is None and call[\"dry_run\"] is dry_run for call in capability.calls)\n        assert observed == []\n        if dry_run:\n            assert ticks == []\n\n    def test_runner_plan_and_empty_configuration_never_invoke_callbacks(\n        self,\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\n    ) -> None:\n        events: list[ProgressEvent] = []\n        ticks: list[int] = []\n        capability = _Capability(lambda _: iter(()))\n        cfg = _config(monkeypatch, capability, (\"docs\", \"docs-old\"))\n        runner = Runner(\n            cfg,\n            on_progress=events.append,\n            on_tick=lambda: ticks.append(1),\n        )\n        assert {entry.label for entry in runner.plan(list(cfg.instances.items()))} == {\"docs\", \"docs-old\"}\n        assert capability.calls == []\n        assert len(capability.plans) == 2\n        empty = Runner(BackupConfig(), on_progress=events.append, on_tick=lambda: ticks.append(1))\n        assert list(empty.run([])) == []\n        assert list(empty.plan([])) == []\n        assert events == []\n        assert ticks == []\n\n    def test_runner_unknown_capability_yields_failure_without_fabricated_progress(\n        self,\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\n    ) -> None:\n        events: list[ProgressEvent] = []\n\n        def produce(kwargs: dict[str, Any]) -> Iterator[StepResult]:\n            for event in _frames(kwargs[\"label\"]):\n                kwargs[\"progress\"](event)\n            yield StepResult(kwargs[\"label\"], True, \"stored\")\n\n        capability = _Capability(produce)\n        cfg = _config(monkeypatch, capability, (\"docs\",))\n        cfg = BackupConfig(instances={**cfg.instances, \"docs-old\": BackupInstance(use=\"controlled-progress-old\")})\n        runner = Runner(cfg, on_progress=events.append)\n        results = {}\n        for result in runner.run(list(cfg.instances.items())):\n            results[result.label] = result\n            if result.label == \"docs\":\n                assert events == _frames(\"docs\")\n        assert results[\"docs\"].success is True\n        assert results[\"docs-old\"].success is False\n        assert results[\"docs-old\"].message\n        assert events == _frames(\"docs\")\n        assert [call[\"label\"] for call in capability.calls] == [\"docs\"]\n\n\nclass TestRunnerCancellation:\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"interrupt\", [False, True])\n    def test_runner_drains_queued_prefix_when_observer_requests_cancel_or_interrupts(\n        self,\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\n        interrupt: bool,\n    ) -> None:\n        queued = threading.Event()\n        finished = threading.Event()\n        received: list[ProgressEvent] = []\n\n        def produce(kwargs: dict[str, Any]) -> Iterator[StepResult]:\n            try:\n                for event in _frames(kwargs[\"label\"])[:2]:\n                    kwargs[\"progress\"](event)\n                queued.set()\n                assert kwargs[\"cancel\"].wait(3), \"cancellation did not reach capability\"\n                kwargs[\"progress\"](_frames(kwargs[\"label\"])[2])\n                yield StepResult(kwargs[\"label\"], False, \"cancelled writer\")\n            finally:\n                finished.set()\n\n        def observe(event: ProgressEvent) -> None:\n            received.append(event)\n            if len(received) == 1:\n                assert queued.wait(2)\n                if interrupt:\n                    raise KeyboardInterrupt\n                runner.request_cancel()\n\n        capability = _Capability(produce)\n        cfg = _config(monkeypatch, capability, (\"cancel-me\",))\n        runner = Runner(cfg, on_progress=observe)\n        results = []\n        for result in runner.run(list(cfg.instances.items())):\n            assert received == _frames(\"cancel-me\")[:2]\n            assert finished.is_set()\n            results.append(result)\n        assert runner.interrupted is True\n        assert [result.label for result in results] == [\"cancel-me\"]\n        assert results[0].success is False\n        assert results[0].message\n        assert received == _frames(\"cancel-me\")[:2]\n\n    def test_runner_uses_fresh_progress_queue_for_each_run(\n        self,\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\n    ) -> None:\n        received: list[ProgressEvent] = []\n        previous_enqueues: list[Callable[[ProgressEvent], None]] = []\n\n        def produce(kwargs: dict[str, Any]) -> Iterator[StepResult]:\n            progress = kwargs[\"progress\"]\n            previous_enqueues.append(progress)\n            for event in _frames(kwargs[\"label\"], 7 if len(previous_enqueues) == 1 else 29):\n                progress(event)\n            yield StepResult(kwargs[\"label\"], True, \"stored\")\n\n        capability = _Capability(produce)\n        cfg = _config(monkeypatch, capability, (\"same-label\",))\n        runner = Runner(cfg, on_progress=received.append)\n        assert _outcomes(runner.run(list(cfg.instances.items()))) == [(\"same-label\", True, \"stored\")]\n        assert received == _frames(\"same-label\", 7)\n        previous_enqueues[0](ProgressEvent(\"same-label-old\", \"archiving\", 999, 1000))\n        received.clear()\n        assert _outcomes(runner.run(list(cfg.instances.items()))) == [(\"same-label\", True, \"stored\")]\n        assert received == _frames(\"same-label\", 29)\n        assert previous_enqueues[0] is not previous_enqueues[1]\n\n\nclass _FloodCapability(_Capability):\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        super().__init__(self.produce_flood)\n        self.start = threading.Event()\n        self.full = threading.Event()\n        self.overflow_attempt = threading.Event()\n        self.overflow_returned = threading.Event()\n        self.finished = threading.Event()\n        self.cancel_seen = threading.Event()\n        self.tick_delivered = threading.Event()\n        self.enqueued: list[ProgressEvent] = []\n\n    def produce_flood(self, kwargs: dict[str, Any]) -> Iterator[StepResult]:\n        label = kwargs[\"label\"]\n        if label == \"first\":\n            yield StepResult(label, True, \"first finished\")\n            return\n        try:\n            assert self.start.wait(3), \"consumer did not release producer\"\n            for number in range(513):\n                if number == 256:\n                    self.full.set()\n                    self.overflow_attempt.set()\n                event = ProgressEvent(label, \"archiving\", number, 513)\n                kwargs[\"progress\"](event)\n                self.enqueued.append(event)\n            self.overflow_returned.set()\n            if kwargs[\"cancel\"].is_set():\n                self.cancel_seen.set()\n                kwargs[\"progress\"](ProgressEvent(\"flood-old\", \"finalizing\", 513, 513))\n            yield StepResult(label, True, \"flood finished\")\n        finally:\n            self.finished.set()\n\n\ndef _suspend_flood(\n    monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\n) -> tuple[_FloodCapability, Runner, Iterator[StepResult], list[ProgressEvent]]:\n    capability = _FloodCapability()\n    received: list[ProgressEvent] = []\n    cfg = _config(monkeypatch, capability, (\"first\", \"flood\"))\n    runner = Runner(\n        cfg,\n        jobs=2,\n        on_progress=received.append,\n        on_tick=capability.tick_delivered.set,\n    )\n    iterator = runner.run(list(cfg.instances.items()))\n    assert _outcomes([next(iterator)]) == [(\"first\", True, \"first finished\")]\n    capability.tick_delivered.clear()\n    capability.start.set()\n    return capability, runner, iterator, received\n\n\ndef _assert_queue_backpressure(capability: _FloodCapability) -> None:\n    assert capability.full.wait(2)\n    assert capability.overflow_attempt.wait(2)\n    assert not capability.overflow_returned.wait(0.45), \"the 257th event bypassed bounded backpressure\"\n    assert len(capability.enqueued) == 256\n    assert not capability.tick_delivered.is_set(), \"ticks ran while the consumer held a yielded result\"\n\n\nclass TestRunnerBoundedQueue:\n    def test_runner_drains_full_queue_without_waiting_for_a_completed_future(\n        self,\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\n    ) -> None:\n        capability, _runner, iterator, received = _suspend_flood(monkeypatch)\n        with closing(iterator):\n            _assert_queue_backpressure(capability)\n            assert received == []\n            remaining = []\n            for result in iterator:\n                assert received == [ProgressEvent(\"flood\", \"archiving\", number, 513) for number in range(513)]\n                remaining.append(result)\n        assert _outcomes(remaining) == [(\"flood\", True, \"flood finished\")]\n        assert capability.finished.is_set()\n        assert capability.overflow_returned.is_set()\n        assert capability.cancel_seen.is_set() is False\n\n    def test_runner_cancel_unblocks_backpressure_and_drains_every_previously_queued_event(\n        self,\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\n    ) -> None:\n        capability, runner, iterator, received = _suspend_flood(monkeypatch)\n        with closing(iterator):\n            _assert_queue_backpressure(capability)\n            runner.request_cancel()\n            assert capability.overflow_returned.wait(2), \"cancelled enqueue kept retrying a full queue\"\n            assert capability.finished.wait(2)\n            remaining = []\n            for result in iterator:\n                assert received == [ProgressEvent(\"flood\", \"archiving\", number, 513) for number in range(256)]\n                remaining.append(result)\n        assert [result.label for result in remaining] == [\"flood\"]\n        assert runner.interrupted is True\n        assert capability.cancel_seen.is_set()\n\n    def test_runner_abandonment_cancels_before_join_and_never_calls_observers_in_finally(\n        self,\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\n    ) -> None:\n        capability, runner, iterator, received = _suspend_flood(monkeypatch)\n        closed = threading.Event()\n        rescue_needed = threading.Event()\n\n        def rescue_blocked_close() -> None:\n            if not closed.wait(1.5):\n                rescue_needed.set()\n                runner.request_cancel()\n\n        _assert_queue_backpressure(capability)\n        rescue = threading.Thread(target=rescue_blocked_close, daemon=True)\n        rescue.start()\n        try:\n            iterator.close()\n        finally:\n            closed.set()\n            runner.request_cancel()\n            rescue.join(timeout=2)\n        assert not rescue_needed.is_set(), \"abandonment joined a producer before cancelling its enqueue\"\n        assert capability.finished.is_set()\n        assert capability.cancel_seen.is_set()\n        assert received == []\n\nFAILED CHECK: precommit Ruff S112 except Exception:continue in _drain_progress, S110 except Exception:pass in tick handler; PLR0917 new sixth positional progress argument to _run_instance. Preserve ordinary observer exception isolation without logging, e.g. contextlib.suppress(Exception). Preserve existing five positional private arguments; make new progress keyword-only and submit it by keyword or use narrowly justified contract noqa. Ruff already auto-fixed two other findings; preserve those valid fixes. All21 new tests previously pass. Change only lint-necessary lines, no test edits/refactoring. Run narrow current selector and ruff check runner.py.\n\n\n## Architecture context\n\n# AGENTS.md\n\nBUVIS gems monorepo. Python toolkit (buvis-pybase + zettel) and CLI tools, shipped as a single PyPI package `buvis-gems`. Supports Python 3.11+.\n\n## Reading these instructions\n\nThis root `AGENTS.md` is the always-on canonical guidance. Some directories also\ncarry their own nested `AGENTS.md` with rules scoped to the code beside them.\nBefore working on files in a directory, discover and read any `AGENTS.md` on the\npath from the repo root down to that directory, and follow it for files in its\nscope. Do this yourself even if your host did not load those files automatically\n— host loading of nested files varies and is not guaranteed (see\n[`docs/dev/architecture/agent-host-support.md`](docs/dev/architecture/agent-host-support.md)).\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```bash\nuv sync --all-groups --all-extras            # install deps\npre-commit install                          # setup hooks\nuv run pytest                               # run tests\nuv run pytest -m snapshot                   # run snapshot tests only (skipped off canonical env)\nuv run pytest --snapshot-update             # regenerate snapshot baselines (local use only)\nuv run mypy src/lib/ src/tools/              # type check\nuv run sphinx-build -b html docs/source docs/build/html  # build docs\n```\n\n## Architecture\n\n```text\nsrc/\n├── lib/buvis/pybase/           # shared library (namespace pkg: no buvis/__init__.py)\n│   ├── adapters/               # jira, console, config adapters\n│   ├── configuration/          # settings/config helpers\n│   ├── filesystem/             # file utilities\n│   ├── formatting/             # output formatting\n│   └── zettel/                 # zettel subsystem\n│       ├── domain/             # entities, services, interfaces, value objects\n│       ├── application/        # use cases\n│       ├── infrastructure/     # formatters, repositories, file parsers\n│       └── integrations/       # jira assemblers\n└── tools/\n    ├── bim/                    # BUVIS InfoMesh CLI (zettel integration)\n    ├── dot/                    # dotfiles manager\n    ├── fctracker/              # foreign currency tracker\n    ├── fren/                   # file renamer toolkit\n    ├── morph/                  # file conversion toolkit\n    ├── muc/                    # music collection tools\n    ├── netscan/                # network scanning tools\n    ├── outlookctl/             # Outlook CLI\n    ├── pinger/                 # ICMP ping utilities\n    ├── puc/                    # photo utility collection\n    ├── readerctl/              # Readwise Reader CLI\n    ├── sysup/                  # system update tools\n    ├── vuc/                    # video utility collection\n    └── zseq/                   # Zettelsequence utilities\ntests/\n├── lib/                        # library tests\n│   ├── pybase/\n│   ├── zettel/\n│   └── zettel_integrations/\n└── tools/                      # CLI tool tests\ntools/                          # Dev command shims (on PATH via mise) + helpers\n├── release                     # public shim → mise `release` task\n└── lib/                        # helpers, invoked by path (NOT on PATH)\n    ├── release                 # release impl: bump+tag+push\n    ├── pin_deps.py             # pin deps from uv.lock for publishing\n    ├── scaffold.py             # scaffold a new tool\n    ├── check_audit_ignores.py  # pip-audit suppression guard (+ audit/ config)\n    ├── check_tool_wiring.py    # pre-commit tool-wiring check\n    ├── parity_brief_portfolio.py\n    └── gen_zettel_writer_fixtures.py\n```\n\n**Key patterns:**\n\n- **Single package**: `buvis-gems` on PyPI, one `uv tool install`\n- **Namespace package**: `src/lib/buvis/` has no `__init__.py`\n- **Hatch packages**: each `src/tools/<name>/` maps to top-level `<name>` in wheel\n- **Libraries are internal**: pybase + zettel not published separately\n- **All-interface rule**: every command/action must work across CLI, TUI, API, and WebUI\n\n## Tool Structure\n\nEvery tool under `src/tools/<name>/` follows a base layout:\n\n```text\ntool_name/\n├── __init__.py\n├── __main__.py\n├── cli.py              # Click entry point\n├── settings.py         # Tool-specific settings\n└── commands/           # One module per CLI command\n```\n\nAdd subdirs only when needed:\n\n| Dir | When | Example |\n|-----|------|---------|\n| `adapters/` | External service clients | fctracker, readerctl |\n| `domain/` | Business logic beyond simple commands | fctracker |\n| `shared/` | Code reused across commands | zseq |\n\n> `bim/commands/serve/frontend/` contains the WebUI SvelteKit app — the only tool with a frontend subtree.\n\n> `bim/commands/doc/` follows the existing `commands/serve/`-style group pattern with a `shared/` subdir holding cross-command utilities (pipeline, OCR/classifier/extractor adapters, state DB, issuer registry, zettel writer).\n\n## Code Conventions\n\n**Type hints** — modern style, no `Optional`:\n\n```python\nfrom __future__ import annotations\ndef foo(path: Path | None = None) -> list[str]: ...\n```\n\n**Imports**:\n\n- Explicit `__all__` in `__init__.py`\n- `TYPE_CHECKING` guards for type-only imports\n\n**Docstrings**: Google format\n\n**CLI pattern**: Click-based. `buvis_options` adds `--version`, `--config`, `--log-level`, `--debug`, and `--update` to every tool automatically:\n\n```python\n@click.command()\n@buvis_options\n@click.pass_context\ndef cli(ctx: click.Context) -> None:\n    settings = get_settings(ctx)\n    ...\n```\n\n**Lazy imports in CLI handlers**: import command classes inside handler functions, not at module level. This avoids pulling in optional/heavy dependencies before the user picks a subcommand:\n\n```python\n@cli.command(\"create\")\n@click.pass_context\ndef create(ctx):\n    from bim.commands.create_note.create_note import CommandCreateNote\n    ...\n```\n\n## Error Handling\n\n**Command layer** (`commands/`):\n- Return `CommandResult` for all outcomes — success and failure\n- Catch expected exceptions (e.g. `FileNotFoundError`) internally, return `CommandResult(success=False, error=str(exc))`\n- No `console.panic()` or `sys.exit()` inside command classes\n- No custom exception classes for control flow\n\n**CLI layer** (`cli.py`):\n- Inspect `CommandResult` and call `console.panic()` / `console.failure()` / `console.success()`\n- Use `console.report_result()` for standardized output\n- Catch `ImportError` for optional deps, call `console.require_import()`\n- Catch `FatalError` for unrecoverable infrastructure failures\n\n**Click argument validation**:\n- Avoid parse-time validators that short-circuit before the callback (`click.Path(exists=True)`, `IntRange`, custom `ParamType.convert` that raises). They emit Click's default `Usage: ... Error: ...` formatting and bypass the buvis console.\n- Validate inside the callback instead: `if not path.is_file(): console.panic(f\"file not found: {path}\"); return`.\n- `click.Choice` is the exception — its parse-time error lists the valid values, which is more useful than a rewritten message.\n\n**Console methods**:\n- Fatal (exit): `console.panic(msg)` — prints + exits with code 1\n- Recoverable: `console.failure(msg)` — prints, continues\n- Status: `console.success()`, `console.warning()`, `console.info()`\n- All user-facing output must route through `console`. No `print()`, `sys.stdout.write()`, `sys.stderr.write()`, `click.echo()`, `click.secho()`, or the Python logging module. Plain writes bypass the buvis prefix markers (`✘`, `✓`, etc.) and become indistinguishable from stray output, which is what makes a missed `console.panic` look like a print statement to the user.\n- The one sanctioned exception is the `dot filter` clean/smudge plumbing, which writes git's blob payload as raw bytes on stdout and at most one error line on stderr, because git owns both streams and a console marker would corrupt the payload (discovery R12).\n- Never let raw exceptions (stack traces) reach the user.\n\n## Invariants (evolution guardrails)\n\nThese encode the failure classes surfaced by the 2026-07-09 evolution assessment (`docs/dev/project-management/reviews/evolution-assessment-2026-07-09.md`). Each is either **HOLDS** (enforce it) or a **GAP** (a tracked PRD is closing it — write new code to the target state, not the current one).\n\n- **Atomic persistence** — never persist a note, state file, or config with a bare `Path.write_text`/`open(...,\"w\")`. Use `pybase.filesystem.atomic_write` (tempfile + fsync + `os.replace`). Truncate-then-write loses data on crash/ENOSPC. *HOLDS for the library and note/updater write paths (00041) — keep it, except `ConfigWriter.write` (`configuration/config_writer.py`), which still does a bare `write_text` — deliberately out of scope for 00041. GAP → pidash was closed by retiring pidash (00071); autopilot-state durability now lives in the buvis home repo (tracon/statectl), not gems.*\n- **Confine request-derived paths** — any filesystem path built from an HTTP request / external input must be `resolve()`d and asserted under an allowed root before read/write/delete/open. Network-facing servers must have auth + `TrustedHostMiddleware`. *HOLDS (00042) — bim serve confines request paths via `confine_path` (403 outside the vault/archive roots), mints a startup token required as `X-Buvis-Token`, installs `TrustedHostMiddleware`, and warns on a non-loopback bind (`commands/serve/_security.py`). Keep it.*\n- **The library stays interface-agnostic** — `src/lib/buvis/pybase/` must not import a UI framework at module import time or emit output outside the console adapter. No import-time Click monkey-patching, no `sys.exit`/`click.echo`/`print` in lib code. A TUI/API/WebUI process must be able to `import` settings without pulling Click. *HOLDS (00052) — keep it.*\n- **One action, one implementation across interfaces** — CLI/TUI/API/WebUI adapters must drive the same command class / use case through the composition root and return `CommandResult`; do not reimplement business logic per interface (dot's TUI is the anti-pattern; bim's serve action registry is the exemplar). *HOLDS (00051 design → 00053/00054) — the all-interface seam design (00051) is realized: dot's git ops unified behind `DotGitService` (00053) and bim's serve/TUI converged on the shared action registry (00054). Keep it.*\n- **Claim/lifecycle release on any exit** — resource claims and locks release in `finally` (or catch `BaseException`), never only `except Exception`; `KeyboardInterrupt` must not leak a claim. *HOLDS (00044) — the bim doc claim/dedup pipeline releases claims and locks in `finally` (`commands/doc/shared/`); keep it.*\n- **`CommandResult` discipline** — commands return `CommandResult`; the CLI/adapter layer renders it (`console.report_result`) and maps exit/HTTP status. No `sys.exit`/`console.panic` inside command classes. *HOLDS in `src/tools/*/commands/**` — keep it.*\n- **Clean-architecture layering + tool isolation** — zettel `domain → application → infrastructure → integrations` one-directional; no cross-tool imports; no `src/lib → src/tools`. *HOLDS — keep it.*\n\n## Testing\n\n- pytest + pytest-mock + pytest-cov\n- Tests in `tests/` mirror `src/lib/` and `src/tools/` structure\n- Mock subprocess calls heavily\n- Class-based test organization\n- **No unused imports/variables**\n- **Markers**: `pytest -m <tool>` runs one tool, `pytest -m lib` runs library tests, `pytest -m \"not bim\"` excludes a tool. Auto-applied by path in `tests/conftest.py` — no decorators needed. Scaffold registers markers for new tools.\n- **Snapshot tests** (`@pytest.mark.snapshot`) only run on the canonical env (Linux + Python 3.12) — SVG output from Rich/Textual differs across OS/Python so baselines must come from one place. Anywhere else they are auto-skipped. To regenerate baselines run the `update-snapshots` GitHub workflow (`gh workflow run update-snapshots.yml`); it runs `pytest --snapshot-update` on the canonical env and commits the result. Force locally with `BUVIS_SNAPSHOT_CANONICAL=1` only if you know what you're doing.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\nuv tool install buvis-gems              # core only (no tool-specific deps)\nuv tool install buvis-gems[bim]         # with jira support\nuv tool install buvis-gems[bim-web]     # bim web UI deps\nuv tool install buvis-gems[all]         # everything\nuv tool upgrade buvis-gems              # update\n```\n\nExtras: `bim`, `bim-web`, `doc`, `dot`, `fren`, `morph`, `muc`, `pinger`, `postup`, `postup-web`, `readerctl`, `all`\n\n## Release\n\n> Full procedure (version authority, checks, destinations, partial-failure recovery): `docs/dev/procedures/releasing.md`.\n\n```bash\nrelease patch|minor|major              # bump, tag, push → CI publishes to PyPI\nrelease --pre rc1                      # pre-release current version to TestPyPI\nrelease --pre rc1 minor                # bump + pre-release to TestPyPI\nrelease                                # after rc: strip suffix, release stable to PyPI\nrelease local                          # build .devN wheel + install locally\nrelease --dry-run [--pre rc1] [patch]  # preview without changes\n```\n\n`mise` adds `tools` to PATH (shims; `tools/lib` holds the implementations). Tags with `rc` in the name publish to TestPyPI; stable tags go to PyPI. Manual workflow dispatch defaults to TestPyPI.\n\n**First-time setup** (already done for buvis-gems):\n- test.pypi.org: add trusted publisher (owner: `buvis`, repo: `gems`, workflow: `publish.yml`, env: `testpypi`)\n- GitHub repo settings: create `testpypi` and `pypi` environments\n\n**Why explicit version in pyproject.toml?** maturin reads the version from `pyproject.toml` at build time to compile the Rust extension. Tag-based versioning (hatch-vcs) would require glue to inject the version before maturin sees it. Pure Python projects like mkdocs-zettelkasten use hatch-vcs instead — the version derives from the git tag, no file to keep in sync, no bump commits.\n\nRelevant reviewed API contracts (not acceptance criteria):\n\n```python\ndef Runner.__init__(\n    self: Runner, cfg: BackupConfig, *, dry_run: bool = False, jobs: int = 3,\n    on_progress: Callable[[ProgressEvent], None] | None = None,\n    on_tick: Callable[[], None] | None = None,\n) -> None: ...\n```\n\nKeep `Runner.run`, `request_cancel`, `plan`, `interrupted` and `cancelled_names` contracts unchanged. `on_tick` is an optional, backward-compatible refinement of the PRD's wake-up requirement: a wake-up with no event needs a distinct hook to recompute elapsed text. Never replay an old `ProgressEvent`, synthesize a heartbeat phase, yield non-results or create a CLI timer thread to implement a tick.\n\nEach `run()` creates a fresh `queue.Queue[ProgressEvent](maxsize=256)` for progress, separate from the existing completed-future queue. The progress queue holds at most 256 events. Workers receive only the enqueue callable as `progress`; they never receive `on_progress`, `on_tick` or a console object. The enqueue callable checks the run's cancellation event, then calls `put(event, timeout=0.2)`; on `queue.Full`, retry while cancellation remains unset. If cancellation becomes set, return without enqueueing or raising. A queue timeout is backpressure, never an archive failure. No event is silently dropped for an uncancelled successful instance. When `on_progress is None` or `dry_run=True`, pass `progress=None` instead. No callbacks are invoked by `plan()`. Suppress both callbacks for dry runs.\n\nWhile work remains pending, drain currently queued progress with `get_nowait()` before waiting for a completion, then use `completed.get(timeout=0.2)`. Catch `queue.Empty` as a normal wake-up, drain progress again, and invoke the optional tick on the iteration thread. Drain on completion notification as well. Drain before every terminal result is yielded, including ready preflight rows and cancellation outcomes, and once after joined workers finish during normal cancellation. These drains unblock bounded-queue producers even when no future has completed. Enqueuing is synchronous inside the capability, before its future completes, so a completed uncancelled instance's entire queued progress prefix is available before its result. Preserve FIFO event order per label. Cross-label event order is queue insertion order and need not equal configured launch order. After cancellation, no new progress enqueue is required; drain every event already queued before terminal cancellation results.\n\nTicks run on the thread advancing `Runner.run`, only while the generator is actively executing. The wait loop offers a tick at least every 0.2 seconds during an otherwise idle wait, subject to scheduler/callback execution time; no guarantee applies while the consumer holds a yielded result or the existing blocking cancellation join runs. A callback must be short and nonblocking. Catch ordinary exceptions from each `on_progress`/`on_tick` invocation separately so one broken observer cannot turn any archive into a failure. Preserve calling-thread `KeyboardInterrupt` handling, request cancellation and drain the same run.\n\nOn generator abandonment, set cancellation before joining writers, so producers blocked on the bounded queue observe cancellation after at most their current 0.2-second put timeout and return. Do not invoke user callbacks from the abandonment-only `finally` path. Normal cancellation likewise sets cancellation before shutdown/join, then drains the joined queue before yielding results. Release per-run queue references on exit. A subsequent run uses clean queues and cannot receive earlier events. Do not refactor outcomes, submission boundaries, lost-notification recovery or cancellation ordering as part of this feature.\nRead-only support modules: /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/gems/src/tools/backup/step_result.py, /Users/bob/git/src/github.