+{"timestamp":"2026-11-01T21:06:07.703Z","ordinal":15,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a198ef-055d-76b1-98d8-2a897c19eae9","turn_id":"01a198ef-059b-7450-b381-0b75b5b59951","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-dbc6e321-41d6-4e22-8359-c04018d763f3","process_id":"30423","command":["/opt/homebrew/bin/bash","-lc","cat docs/dev/tmp/dispatch-tess-3.txt"],"cwd":"file:///Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/gems","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"cat docs/dev/tmp/dispatch-tess-3.txt","name":"dispatch-tess-3.txt","path":"docs/dev/tmp/dispatch-tess-3.txt"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"You are writing tests for a feature. You have NOT seen any implementation and must NOT think about how to implement it.\n\nTask: Deliver runner progress on calling thread\n\nDescription:\nDeliver runner progress on calling thread\n\nLocation: /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/gems/src/tools/backup/runner.py\n\nReuse: Existing NamedTuple records, archive writers, completion queue, pending-result reporting and console.status as identified in reviewed design.\n\nContract (verbatim — reviewed design):\n```python\ndef Runner.__init__(\n    self: Runner, cfg: BackupConfig, *, dry_run: bool = False, jobs: int = 3,\n    on_progress: Callable[[ProgressEvent], None] | None = None,\n    on_tick: Callable[[], None] | None = None,\n) -> None: ...\n```\n\nKeep `Runner.run`, `request_cancel`, `plan`, `interrupted` and `cancelled_names` contracts unchanged. `on_tick` is an optional, backward-compatible refinement of the PRD's wake-up requirement: a wake-up with no event needs a distinct hook to recompute elapsed text. Never replay an old `ProgressEvent`, synthesize a heartbeat phase, yield non-results or create a CLI timer thread to implement a tick.\n\nEach `run()` creates a fresh `queue.Queue[ProgressEvent](maxsize=256)` for progress, separate from the existing completed-future queue. The progress queue holds at most 256 events. Workers receive only the enqueue callable as `progress`; they never receive `on_progress`, `on_tick` or a console object. The enqueue callable checks the run's cancellation event, then calls `put(event, timeout=0.2)`; on `queue.Full`, retry while cancellation remains unset. If cancellation becomes set, return without enqueueing or raising. A queue timeout is backpressure, never an archive failure. No event is silently dropped for an uncancelled successful instance. When `on_progress is None` or `dry_run=True`, pass `progress=None` instead. No callbacks are invoked by `plan()`. Suppress both callbacks for dry runs.\n\nWhile work remains pending, drain currently queued progress with `get_nowait()` before waiting for a completion, then use `completed.get(timeout=0.2)`. Catch `queue.Empty` as a normal wake-up, drain progress again, and invoke the optional tick on the iteration thread. Drain on completion notification as well. Drain before every terminal result is yielded, including ready preflight rows and cancellation outcomes, and once after joined workers finish during normal cancellation. These drains unblock bounded-queue producers even when no future has completed. Enqueuing is synchronous inside the capability, before its future completes, so a completed uncancelled instance's entire queued progress prefix is available before its result. Preserve FIFO event order per label. Cross-label event order is queue insertion order and need not equal configured launch order. After cancellation, no new progress enqueue is required; drain every event already queued before terminal cancellation results.\n\nTicks run on the thread advancing `Runner.run`, only while the generator is actively executing. The wait loop offers a tick at least every 0.2 seconds during an otherwise idle wait, subject to scheduler/callback execution time; no guarantee applies while the consumer holds a yielded result or the existing blocking cancellation join runs. A callback must be short and nonblocking. Catch ordinary exceptions from each `on_progress`/`on_tick` invocation separately so one broken observer cannot turn any archive into a failure. Preserve calling-thread `KeyboardInterrupt` handling, request cancellation and drain the same run.\n\nOn generator abandonment, set cancellation before joining writers, so producers blocked on the bounded queue observe cancellation after at most their current 0.2-second put timeout and return. Do not invoke user callbacks from the abandonment-only `finally` path. Normal cancellation likewise sets cancellation before shutdown/join, then drains the joined queue before yielding results. Release per-run queue references on exit. A subsequent run uses clean queues and cannot receive earlier events. Do not refactor outcomes, submission boundaries, lost-notification recovery or cancellation ordering as part of this feature.\n\nDetails:\n- Add focused tests to /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/gems/tests/tools/backup/test_progress.py. Preserve earlier tasks' tests. Use names matching this acceptance selector. If splitting for 800-line limit, use non-collected sibling progress_*_cases.py and import test classes into test_progress.py.\n- Test failure, empty/unknown values and cancellation behavior where applicable; preserve previous interfaces.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- uv run pytest tests/tools/backup/test_progress.py -k \"runner or calling_thread or drain\" -q passes.\n\nVerify: uv run pytest tests/tools/backup/test_progress.py -k \"runner or calling_thread or drain\" -q\nOnly write /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/gems/tests/tools/backup/test_progress.py and split sibling progress_*_cases.py if necessary. Read-only context: /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/gems/tests/tools/backup/test_skip_outcomes.py. Never read implementation files.\n\n\nAcceptance Criteria:\n\n- uv run pytest tests/tools/backup/test_progress.py -k \"runner or calling_thread or drain\" -q passes.\n\nVerify: uv run pytest tests/tools/backup/test_progress.py -k \"runner or calling_thread or drain\" -q\n\nExisting test patterns (follow these conventions):\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom backup.capabilities.tar_archive import TarArchive\nfrom backup.step_result import StepResult\n\n\nclass TestStepResult:\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"label,message\", [(\"first\", \"missing source\"), (\"second\", \"no selected items\")])\n    def test_step_result_keeps_positional_fields_and_defaults_to_not_skipped(self, label: str, message: str) -> None:\n        result = StepResult(label, True, message, None)\n        assert result.label == label\n        assert result.success is True\n        assert result.message == message\n        assert result.archive is None\n        assert result.skipped is False\n        skipped = StepResult(label, True, message, skipped=True)\n        assert skipped.label == label\n        assert skipped.message == message\n        assert skipped.success is True\n        assert skipped.skipped is True\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"engine\", [\"python-tarfile\", \"system-tar\"])\nclass TestSkippedArchives:\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"dry_run\", [False, True])\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"source_state\", [\"missing\", \"file\"])\n    def test_missing_source_skips_but_existing_non_directory_fails(\n        self,\n        tmp_path: Path,\n        engine: str,\n        dry_run: bool,\n        source_state: str,\n    ) -> None:\n        source = tmp_path / source_state\n        if source_state == \"file\":\n            source.write_text(\"not a directory\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        out = tmp_path / \"out.tar.gz\"\n        out.write_bytes(b\"old archive\")\n        before = out.stat()\n        result = next(\n            iter(\n                TarArchive().run(\n                    label=\"optional\",\n                    source=str(source),\n                    out=str(out),\n                    engine=engine,\n                    dry_run=dry_run,\n                )\n            )\n        )\n        assert result.success is (source_state == \"missing\")\n        assert result.skipped is (source_state == \"missing\")\n        reason = \"source not found\" if source_state == \"missing\" else \"source is not a directory\"\n        assert result.message == f\"{reason}: {source}\"\n        assert out.read_bytes() == b\"old archive\"\n        assert out.stat().st_mtime_ns == before.st_mtime_ns\n        assert out.stat().st_ino == before.st_ino\n        assert sorted(path.name for path in tmp_path.iterdir()) == sorted(\n            [\"out.tar.gz\", \"file\"] if source_state == \"file\" else [\"out.tar.gz\"],\n        )\n\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"dry_run\", [False, True])\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"kind\", [\"absent\", \"excluded\"])\n    def test_no_selected_members_skips_and_preserves_existing_output(\n        self,\n        tmp_path: Path,\n        engine: str,\n        dry_run: bool,\n        kind: str,\n    ) -> None:\n        source = tmp_path / \"src\"\n        source.mkdir()\n        (source / \"unselected\").write_text(\"must not leak\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        if kind == \"excluded\":\n            (source / \"a\").write_text(\"first\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n            (source / \"b\").write_text(\"second\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        out = tmp_path / \"out.tar.gz\"\n        out.write_bytes(b\"preserve previous\")\n        before = out.stat()\n        result = next(\n            iter(\n                TarArchive().run(\n                    label=\"optional\",\n                    source=str(source),\n                    out=str(out),\n                    items=[\"a\", \"b\"],\n                    excludes=[\"a\", \"b\"],\n                    engine=engine,\n                    dry_run=dry_run,\n                )\n            )\n        )\n        assert result.success is True\n        assert result.skipped is True\n        assert result.message\n        assert out.read_bytes() == b\"preserve previous\"\n        assert out.stat().st_mtime_ns == before.st_mtime_ns\n        assert out.stat().st_ino == before.st_ino\n        assert sorted(path.name for path in tmp_path.iterdir()) == [\"out.tar.gz\", \"src\"]\n\n\nPublic interfaces/types relevant to this task:\n\n```python\ndef Runner.__init__(\n    self: Runner, cfg: BackupConfig, *, dry_run: bool = False, jobs: int = 3,\n    on_progress: Callable[[ProgressEvent], None] | None = None,\n    on_tick: Callable[[], None] | None = None,\n) -> None: ...\n```\n\nKeep `Runner.run`, `request_cancel`, `plan`, `interrupted` and `cancelled_names` contracts unchanged. `on_tick` is an optional, backward-compatible refinement of the PRD's wake-up requirement: a wake-up with no event needs a distinct hook to recompute elapsed text. Never replay an old `ProgressEvent`, synthesize a heartbeat phase, yield non-results or create a CLI timer thread to implement a tick.\n\nEach `run()` creates a fresh `queue.Queue[ProgressEvent](maxsize=256)` for progress, separate from the existing completed-future queue. The progress queue holds at most 256 events. Workers receive only the enqueue callable as `progress`; they never receive `on_progress`, `on_tick` or a console object. The enqueue callable checks the run's cancellation event, then calls `put(event, timeout=0.2)`; on `queue.Full`, retry while cancellation remains unset. If cancellation becomes set, return without enqueueing or raising. A queue timeout is backpressure, never an archive failure. No event is silently dropped for an uncancelled successful instance. When `on_progress is None` or `dry_run=True`, pass `progress=None` instead. No callbacks are invoked by `plan()`. Suppress both callbacks for dry runs.\n\nWhile work remains pending, drain currently queued progress with `get_nowait()` before waiting for a completion, then use `completed.get(timeout=0.2)`. Catch `queue.Empty` as a normal wake-up, drain progress again, and invoke the optional tick 