+{"timestamp":"2026-11-01T21:06:56.853Z","ordinal":60,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a198ef-055d-76b1-98d8-2a897c19eae9","turn_id":"01a198ef-059b-7450-b381-0b75b5b59951","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-a0e01fc1-2839-4e3c-9fbe-d84b57738308","process_id":"9455","command":["/opt/homebrew/bin/bash","-lc","python -c 'import subprocess; subprocess.run([\"rg\", \"-n\", \"^\", \"/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md\", \"/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md\"], check=True, timeout=60)'"],"cwd":"file:///Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/gems","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python -c 'import subprocess; subprocess.run([\"rg\", \"-n\", \"^\", \"/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md\", \"/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md\"], check=True, timeout=60)'"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:1:---\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:2:name: python-testing\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:3:description: Use when writing, fixing, or reviewing Python tests with pytest. Covers TDD, fixtures, mocking, parametrization, coverage. Triggers on \"pytest\", \"python test\", \"conftest\", \"pytest.mark\", \"parametrize\", \"pytest fixture\", \"python mock\".\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:4:compatibility: \"Portable standalone compatibility copy of the strunk plugin skill for agents without that plugin; Claude Code uses the namespaced plugin skill.\"\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:5:---\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:6:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:7:# Python Testing\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:8:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:9:TDD: write the failing test (RED), make it pass (GREEN), refactor. One behavior per test. No logic in tests. Coverage target 80%, higher on critical paths.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:10:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:11:## Rulings\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:12:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:13:**Mocking**\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:14:- Patch where the name is *used*, not where it's defined: `@patch(\"myapp.service.requests\")`, not `@patch(\"requests\")`.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:15:- `autospec=True` so the mock rejects calls the real API would reject.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:16:- Mock at the boundary (I/O, network, clock). Never mock the thing under test.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:17:- Async: assert with `assert_awaited_once()`, not `assert_called_once()`.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:18:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:19:**Fixtures**\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:20:- `yield` for teardown; the line after `yield` is the cleanup.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:21:- Default to function scope. Widen to `module`/`session` only for genuinely expensive resources.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:22:- `autouse` hides dependencies — use sparingly; prefer explicit injection.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:23:- `tmp_path` for temp files (auto-cleanup, `Path` API), not `tempfile`.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:24:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:25:**Parametrize**\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:26:- `@pytest.mark.parametrize` over loops — distinct test IDs, filterable with `-k`.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:27:- Pass `ids=[...]` when params are objects or tuples; pytest already auto-names plain str/int/bool readably.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:28:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:29:**Config**\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:30:- One config in `pyproject.toml` (`[tool.pytest.ini_options]`), not a separate `pytest.ini`.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:31:- `--strict-markers` so a typo'd marker fails instead of silently passing.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:32:- Register custom markers — e.g. `slow`, `@pytest.mark.unit`, `@pytest.mark.integration` — so `--strict-markers` catches a typo.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:33:- Coverage locally: `pytest --cov=src --cov-report=term-missing` — the missing-line report is the point; a bare percentage is not actionable.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:34:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:35:**Async (pytest-asyncio)**\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:36:- Default mode is `strict`: an async test with no `@pytest.mark.asyncio` is silently not collected. Set `asyncio_mode = \"auto\"` in `[tool.pytest.ini_options]` to drop the per-test marker.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md:37:- Use `@pytest_asyncio.fixture` for async fixtures in strict mode.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:1:---\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:2:name: python-patterns\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:3:description: Use when writing, reviewing, or refactoring Python code. Covers idioms, naming, traps, toolchain, and security. Triggers on Python file edits, \"pythonic\", \"PEP 8\", \"python best practices\", \"python idioms\", \"bandit\".\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:4:compatibility: \"Portable standalone compatibility copy of the strunk plugin skill for agents without that plugin; Claude Code uses the namespaced plugin skill.\"\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:5:---\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:6:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:7:# Python Patterns\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:8:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:9:Pick a side. These are the rulings, not a tutorial.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:10:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:11:## Idioms that earn their place\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:12:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:13:| Rule | Why |\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:14:|------|-----|\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:15:| `X \\| Y`, not `Union[X, Y]` | 3.10+ runtime syntax; clearer. On 3.9 it parses only under `from __future__ import annotations` and still breaks `get_type_hints`/`isinstance` — keep `Optional`/`Union` if you support 3.9. |\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:16:| `Protocol`, not `ABC`, for duck typing | Structural typing; no inheritance you don't control. |\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:17:| `@dataclass(frozen=True)` for immutable records, plain `dataclass` only when you must mutate, `NamedTuple` for lightweight immutable rows | Pydantic only when you need validation. |\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:18:| `raise New(...) from e` | Marks the explicit cause. A bare `raise New()` still chains implicitly (\"During handling...\"); use `from None` to suppress. |\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:19:| `@functools.wraps` on every decorator | Without it the wrapper loses `__name__`, `__doc__`, signature. |\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:20:| `pathlib.Path`, not `os.path` | One object, no string surgery. |\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:21:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:22:## Naming (PEP 8)\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:23:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:24:`snake_case` for modules, functions, variables. `CapWords` for classes. `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` for constants. Leading `_` for internal names.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:25:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:26:**Never name a `.py` file in kebab-case.** `my-script.py` is not importable (`import my-script` is a `SyntaxError`). Kebab-case belongs only in the `pyproject.toml` distribution name and the CLI command, both of which map to a `snake_case` module.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:27:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:28:## Traps\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:29:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:30:```python\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:31:# Mutable default argument — shared across calls\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:32:def bad(items=[]): ...\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:33:def good(items=None):\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:34:    items = [] if items is None else items\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:35:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:36:# Bare except — swallows SystemExit, KeyboardInterrupt\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:37:try: ...\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:38:except Exception as e: ...        # name the exception\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:39:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:40:# __slots__ kills __dict__ and dynamic attributes — use only on fixed,\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:41:# memory-sensitive classes you won't extend.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:42:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:43:# __double_leading is name-mangled to _Class__double_leading.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:44:# Surprises you in subclasses, pickling, and monkey-patching.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:45:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:46:if value is None: ...             # never == None\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:47:```\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:48:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:49:Avoid `from module import *`. Use `isinstance`, never `type(x) ==`.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:50:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:51:## Toolchain\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:52:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:53:**black** to format, **isort** for imports, **ruff** to lint. Type annotations on every function signature — no exceptions for \"obvious\" returns.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:54:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:55:## Resources and laziness\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:56:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:57:Context managers (`with`) for anything holding a resource. Generators for lazy iteration over anything you would otherwise materialize into a list.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:58:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:59:## Security\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:60:\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:61:- Read secrets with `os.environ[\"API_KEY\"]`, never `.get()` — a missing secret must raise `KeyError` at startup, not surface as `None` at request time.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:62:- `python-dotenv` loads a local `.env` in development only. Never commit one.\n/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md:63:- `bandit -r src/` for static security analysis.\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":9500}},"started_at_ms":1793567216853,"completed_at_ms":1793567216853}}
