+{"timestamp":"2026-11-01T21:30:06.138Z","ordinal":16,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a19905-07ba-7213-bb42-a4a07f6c9304","call_id":"call_7a601120b2034c989a2216f8663c759c","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"You are writing tests for a feature. You have NOT seen any implementation and must NOT think about how to implement it.\n\nTask: Render live progress and quiet mode\n\nDescription:\nRender live progress and quiet mode\n\nLocation: /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/gems/src/tools/backup/cli.py\n\nReuse: Existing NamedTuple records, archive writers, completion queue, pending-result reporting and console.status as identified in reviewed design.\n\nContract (verbatim — reviewed design):\n```python\n@click.option(\"--quiet\", is_flag=True, help=\"Hide live progress; keep final results and the summary.\")\n\ndef _format_progress(event: ProgressEvent, elapsed: float) -> str: ...\n\nclass _LiveProgress:\n    def on_progress(self, event: ProgressEvent) -> None: ...\n    def refresh(self) -> None: ...\n    def finish(self, label: str) -> None: ...\n    def close(self) -> None: ...\n\ndef _report_steps(\n    steps: Iterable[StepResult], *, dry_run: bool = False,\n    on_interrupt: Callable[[], None] | None = None,\n    on_result: Callable[[StepResult], None] | None = None,\n) -> bool: ...\n\ndef _run_plan(\n    cfg: BackupConfig, plan: list[tuple[str, BackupInstance]], *,\n    dry_run: bool, plan_only: bool, jobs: int = 3, quiet: bool = False,\n) -> bool: ...\n```\n\nAdd `quiet: bool` to the Click callback and forward it to `_run_plan`. Live mode is exactly `not quiet and sys.stdout.isatty() and not dry_run and not plan_only`; use stdout as the explicit functional contract specifies, even though introductory PRD wording mentions stderr/stdout. Existing list/show-excludes early returns never construct live status. In every disabled mode, construct no status and pass `on_progress=None`, `on_tick=None` to `Runner`.\n\n`_format_progress` returns `label phase [NN%] M:SS` when both byte fields exist, `total_bytes > 0` and `phase != \"finalizing\"`; `NN = min(99, done_bytes * 100 // total_bytes)`. Otherwise omit the percentage and its surrounding space. Brackets are literal display characters. Elapsed seconds are `max(0, int(elapsed))`, formatted with `divmod(seconds, 60)`; minutes can exceed 59 and seconds always have two digits. Examples: `docs archiving [37%] 1:05`, `git scanning 0:02`, `git finalizing 2:00`.\n\n`_LiveProgress` stores latest events and first-seen `time.monotonic()` timestamps by label, in first-event insertion order. Waiting/unsubmitted instances are not active. Phase changes preserve the first timestamp. `on_progress` replaces the label's latest event and refreshes; `refresh` joins active strings with `\" | \"` and calls `Status.update`. Use `rich.text.Text` for the rendered string passed to `Status.update` so configured labels and literal percentage brackets cannot be parsed as Rich markup. Only CLI owns Rich imports and status objects.\n\nCreate at most one `console.status(\"\")` object per live run, lazily at the first event, and start it only while active labels exist. Stop it when the last active label finishes; restart the same object if later submitted work emits its first event. `finish(label)` removes the label and timestamp idempotently and refreshes the remaining jobs. `close()` stops the status idempotently. No status is needed for an empty run or only preflight failures.\n\nCall `_report_steps(..., on_result=lambda step: live.finish(step.label))` in live mode. The report loop invokes `on_result(pending)` immediately before `_report_step(pending)` inside its existing interrupt-handling boundary. Keep the pending result and counters across rendering retries; `finish` is idempotent, and each result still affects counters once. A completed/failed/skipped/cancelled label disappears before its final line prints. Keep `_report_step`, final messages, summary counts and ordinary exit codes unchanged. `--quiet` suppresses redraws only; every result, skip, failure and summary remains visible.\n\nUse `finally` in `_run_plan` to close the original runner generator and the live status on every exit. Preserve the existing retained-iterator interrupt path and exit-130 message. Status updates interrupted by `KeyboardInterrupt` reach the runner or report-loop cancellation owner; cleanup must not leave a spinner or active writer running. Do not move execution into a UI thread.\n\nDetails:\n- Add focused tests to /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/gems/tests/tools/backup/test_progress.py. Preserve earlier tasks' tests. Use names matching this acceptance selector. If splitting for 800-line limit, use non-collected sibling progress_*_cases.py and import test classes into test_progress.py.\n- Test failure, empty/unknown values and cancellation behavior where applicable; preserve previous interfaces.\n\nAcceptance criteria:\n- uv run pytest tests/tools/backup/test_progress.py -k \"cli or quiet or format\" -q passes.\n\nVerify: uv run pytest tests/tools/backup/test_progress.py -k \"cli or quiet or format\" -q\n\nAdditional PRD acceptance criteria (verbatim):\n- `test_no_live_output_when_not_a_tty_or_quiet` passes: final result lines and the summary are still printed.\n\nOnly write /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/gems/tests/tools/backup/test_progress.py and split sibling progress_*_cases.py if necessary. Read-only context: /Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/gems/tests/tools/backup/test_skip_outcomes.py. Never read implementation files.\n\n\nAcceptance Criteria:\n\n- uv run pytest tests/tools/backup/test_progress.py -k \"cli or quiet or format\" -q passes.\n\nVerify: uv run pytest tests/tools/backup/test_progress.py -k \"cli or quiet or format\" -q\n\nAdditional PRD acceptance criteria (verbatim):\n- `test_no_live_output_when_not_a_tty_or_quiet` passes: final result lines and the summary are still printed.\n\n\nExisting test patterns (follow these conventions):\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom backup.capabilities.tar_archive import TarArchive\nfrom backup.step_result import StepResult\n\n\nclass TestStepResult:\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"label,message\", [(\"first\", \"missing source\"), (\"second\", \"no selected items\")])\n    def test_step_result_keeps_positional_fields_and_defaults_to_not_skipped(self, label: str, message: str) -> None:\n        result = StepResult(label, True, message, None)\n        assert result.label == label\n        assert result.success is True\n        assert result.message == message\n        assert result.archive is None\n        assert result.skipped is False\n        skipped = StepResult(label, True, message, skipped=True)\n        assert skipped.label == label\n        assert skipped.message == message\n        assert skipped.success is True\n        assert skipped.skipped is True\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"engine\", [\"python-tarfile\", \"system-tar\"])\nclass TestSkippedArchives:\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"dry_run\", [False, True])\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"source_state\", [\"missing\", \"file\"])\n    def test_missing_source_skips_but_existing_non_directory_fails(\n        self,\n        tmp_path: Path,\n        engine: str,\n        dry_run: bool,\n        source_state: str,\n    ) -> None:\n        source = tmp_path / source_state\n        if source_state == \"file\":\n            source.write_text(\"not a directory\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        out = tmp_path / \"out.tar.gz\"\n        out.write_bytes(b\"old archive\")\n        before = out.stat()\n        result = next(\n            iter(\n                TarArchive().run(\n                    label=\"optional\",\n                    source=str(source),\n                    out=str(out),\n                    engine=engine,\n                    dry_run=dry_run,\n                )\n            )\n        )\n        assert result.success is (source_state == \"missing\")\n        assert result.skipped is (source_state == \"missing\")\n        reason = \"source not found\" if source_state == \"missing\" else \"source is not a directory\"\n        assert result.message == f\"{reason}: {source}\"\n        assert out.read_bytes() == b\"old archive\"\n        assert out.stat().st_mtime_ns == before.st_mtime_ns\n        assert out.stat().st_ino == before.st_ino\n        assert sorted(path.name for path in tmp_path.iterdir()) == sorted(\n            [\"out.tar.gz\", \"file\"] if source_state == \"file\" else [\"out.tar.gz\"],\n        )\n\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"dry_run\", [False, True])\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"kind\", [\"absent\", \"excluded\"])\n    def test_no_selected_members_skips_and_preserves_existing_output(\n        self,\n        tmp_path: Path,\n        engine: str,\n        dry_run: bool,\n        kind: str,\n    ) -> None:\n        source = tmp_path / \"src\"\n        source.mkdir()\n        (source / \"unselected\").write_text(\"must not leak\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        if kind == \"excluded\":\n            (source / \"a\").write_text(\"first\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n            (source / \"b\").write_text(\"second\", encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        out = tmp_path / \"out.tar.gz\"\n        out.write_bytes(b\"preserve previous\")\n        before = out.stat()\n        result = next(\n            iter(\n                TarArchive().run(\n                    label=\"optional\",\n                    source=str(source),\n                    out=str(out),\n                    items=[\"a\", \"b\"],\n                    excludes=[\"a\", \"b\"],\n                    engine=engine,\n                    dry_run=dry_run,\n                )\n            )\n        )\n        assert result.success is True\n        assert result.skipped is True\n        assert result.message\n        assert out.read_bytes() == b\"preserve previous\"\n        assert out.stat().st_mtime_ns == before.st_mtime_ns\n        assert out.stat().st_ino == before.st_ino\n        assert sorted(path.name for path in tmp_path.iterdir()) == [\"out.tar.gz\", \"src\"]\n\n\nPublic interfaces/types relevant to this task:\n\n```python\n@click.option(\"--quiet\", is_flag=True, help=\"Hide live progress; keep final results and the summary.\")\n\ndef _format_progress(event: ProgressEvent, elapsed: float) -> str: ...\n\nclass _LiveProgress:\n    def on_progress(self, event: ProgressEvent) -> None: ...\n    def refresh(self) -> None: ...\n    def finish(self, label: str) -> None: ...\n    def close(self) -> None: ...\n\ndef _report_steps(\n    steps: Iterable[StepResult], *, dry_run: bool = False,\n    on_interrupt: Callable[[], None] | None = None,\n    on_result: Callable[[StepResult], None] | None = None,\n) -> bool: ...\n\ndef _run_plan(\n    cfg: BackupConfig, plan: list[tuple[str, BackupInstance]], *,\n    dry_run: bool, plan_only: bool, jobs: int = 3, quiet: bool = False,\n) -> bool: ...\n```\n\nAdd `quiet: bool` to the Click callback and forward it to `_run_plan`. Live mode is exactly `not quiet and sys.stdout.isatty() and not dry_run and not plan_only`; use stdout as the explicit functional contract specifies, even though introductory PRD wording mentions stderr/stdout. Existing list/show-excludes early returns never construct live status. In every disabled mode, construct no status and pass `on_progress=None`, `on_tick=None` to `Runner`.\n\n`_format_progress` returns `label phase [NN%] M:SS` when both byte fields exist, `total_bytes > 0` and `phase != \"finalizing\"`; `NN = min(99, done_bytes * 100 // total_bytes)`. Otherwise omit the percentage and its surrounding space. Brackets are literal display characters. Elapsed seconds are `max(0, int(elapsed))`, formatted with `divmod(seconds, 60)`; minutes can exceed 59 and seconds always have two digits. Examples: `docs archiving [37%] 1:05`, `git scanni