er running. Do not move execution into a UI thread.\nExisting public configuration declarations:\nclass BackupInstance(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"One configured backup capability instance.\n\n    ``use`` names a registered capability, ``with:`` supplies its inputs, and\n    ``tags`` group instances for ``--tag`` selection. ``enabled: false`` skips\n    the instance without deleting it.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    model_config = ConfigDict(extra=\"forbid\", frozen=True, populate_by_name=True)\n\n    use: str\n    enabled: bool = True\n    order: int = 100\n    tags: tuple[str, ...] = ()\n    inherit_excludes: bool = True\n    exclude_add: tuple[str, ...] = ()\n    exclude_remove: tuple[str, ...] = ()\n    with_: dict[str, object] = Field(default_factory=dict, alias=\"with\")\n\n\nclass BackupConfig(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"The whole merged, validated backup configuration.\n\n    ``instances`` is a name-keyed map of capability instances; ``excludes`` is\n    the global basename exclude list that layers via 00080's ``excludes+`` /\n    ``excludes-`` directives across gem -> user -> machine config.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    model_config = ConfigDict(extra=\"forbid\", frozen=True)\n\n    instances: dict[str, BackupInstance] = {}\n    excludes: tuple[str, ...] = ()\n\nStepResult(label: str, success: bool, message: str = \"\", archive: ArchiveMeta | None = None, *, skipped: bool = False). ArchiveMeta(out_path: str, file_count: int, total_bytes: int). PlanEntry(label: str, source: str, out: str, status: str, reason: str, replaces: bool). ProgressEvent(label, phase, done_bytes, total_bytes).\n\nCapability protocol: inputs property Mapping[str, object]; plan(**kwargs: object) -> PlanEntry; run(**kwargs: object) -> Iterator[StepResult]. Registry backup.capabilities.CAPABILITIES: dict[str, Capability], initially tar-archive. Controlled fake capabilities at this public registry boundary are permitted; never mock Runner itself for runner tests.\n\nPublic import paths: BackupConfig, BackupInstance from