+{"timestamp":"2026-11-01T21:44:02.410Z","ordinal":24,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a19911-9d1d-7123-9b3c-3a61850a9b53","turn_id":"01a19911-9d53-7d91-a68b-f3d8eea901b2","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-e32a213f-79b6-453c-99df-f190661fe0b1","process_id":"85719","command":["/opt/homebrew/bin/bash","-lc","python -c \"from pathlib import Path; paths=[Path('/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md'),Path('/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md'),Path('tests/AGENTS.md'),Path('tests/tools/AGENTS.md'),Path('tests/tools/backup/AGENTS.md'),Path('tests/tools/backup/progress_cli_cases.py')]; [(print('\\nFILE '+str(p)+'\\n'+p.read_text())) for p in paths if p.exists()]\""],"cwd":"file:///Users/bob/git/src/github.com/buvis/gems","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"unknown","cmd":"python -c \"from pathlib import Path; paths=[Path('/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md'),Path('/Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md'),Path('tests/AGENTS.md'),Path('tests/tools/AGENTS.md'),Path('tests/tools/backup/AGENTS.md'),Path('tests/tools/backup/progress_cli_cases.py')]; [(print('\\nFILE '+str(p)+'\\n'+p.read_text())) for p in paths if p.exists()]\""}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","aggregated_output":"\nFILE /Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md\n---\nname: python-patterns\ndescription: Use when writing, reviewing, or refactoring Python code. Covers idioms, naming, traps, toolchain, and security. Triggers on Python file edits, \"pythonic\", \"PEP 8\", \"python best practices\", \"python idioms\", \"bandit\".\ncompatibility: \"Portable standalone compatibility copy of the strunk plugin skill for agents without that plugin; Claude Code uses the namespaced plugin skill.\"\n---\n\n# Python Patterns\n\nPick a side. These are the rulings, not a tutorial.\n\n## Idioms that earn their place\n\n| Rule | Why |\n|------|-----|\n| `X \\| Y`, not `Union[X, Y]` | 3.10+ runtime syntax; clearer. On 3.9 it parses only under `from __future__ import annotations` and still breaks `get_type_hints`/`isinstance` — keep `Optional`/`Union` if you support 3.9. |\n| `Protocol`, not `ABC`, for duck typing | Structural typing; no inheritance you don't control. |\n| `@dataclass(frozen=True)` for immutable records, plain `dataclass` only when you must mutate, `NamedTuple` for lightweight immutable rows | Pydantic only when you need validation. |\n| `raise New(...) from e` | Marks the explicit cause. A bare `raise New()` still chains implicitly (\"During handling...\"); use `from None` to suppress. |\n| `@functools.wraps` on every decorator | Without it the wrapper loses `__name__`, `__doc__`, signature. |\n| `pathlib.Path`, not `os.path` | One object, no string surgery. |\n\n## Naming (PEP 8)\n\n`snake_case` for modules, functions, variables. `CapWords` for classes. `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` for constants. Leading `_` for internal names.\n\n**Never name a `.py` file in kebab-case.** `my-script.py` is not importable (`import my-script` is a `SyntaxError`). Kebab-case belongs only in the `pyproject.toml` distribution name and the CLI command, both of which map to a `snake_case` module.\n\n## Traps\n\n```python\n# Mutable default argument — shared across calls\ndef bad(items=[]): ...\ndef good(items=None):\n    items = [] if items is None else items\n\n# Bare except — swallows SystemExit, KeyboardInterrupt\ntry: ...\nexcept Exception as e: ...        # name the exception\n\n# __slots__ kills __dict__ and dynamic attributes — use only on fixed,\n# memory-sensitive classes you won't extend.\n\n# __double_leading is name-mangled to _Class__double_leading.\n# Surprises you in subclasses, pickling, and monkey-patching.\n\nif value is None: ...             # never == None\n```\n\nAvoid `from module import *`. Use `isinstance`, never `type(x) ==`.\n\n## Toolchain\n\n**black** to format, **isort** for imports, **ruff** to lint. Type annotations on every function signature — no exceptions for \"obvious\" returns.\n\n## Resources and laziness\n\nContext managers (`with`) for anything holding a resource. Generators for lazy iteration over anything you would otherwise materialize into a list.\n\n## Security\n\n- Read secrets with `os.environ[\"API_KEY\"]`, never `.get()` — a missing secret must raise `KeyError` at startup, not surface as `None` at request time.\n- `python-dotenv` loads a local `.env` in development only. Never commit one.\n- `bandit -r src/` for static security analysis.\n\n\nFILE /Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md\n---\nname: python-testing\ndescription: Use when writing, fixing, or reviewing Python tests with pytest. Covers TDD, fixtures, mocking, parametrization, coverage. Triggers on \"pytest\", \"python test\", \"conftest\", \"pytest.mark\", \"parametrize\", \"pytest fixture\", \"python mock\".\ncompatibility: \"Portable standalone compatibility copy of the strunk plugin skill for agents without that plugin; Claude Code uses the namespaced plugin skill.\"\n---\n\n# Python Testing\n\nTDD: write the failing test (RED), make it pass (GREEN), refactor. One behavior per test. No logic in tests. Coverage target 80%, higher on critical paths.\n\n## Rulings\n\n**Mocking**\n- Patch where the name is *used*, not where it's defined: `@patch(\"myapp.service.requests\")`, not `@patch(\"requests\")`.\n- `autospec=True` so the mock rejects calls the real API would reject.\n- Mock at the boundary (I/O, network, clock). Never mock the thing under test.\n- Async: assert with `assert_awaited_once()`, not `assert_called_once()`.\n\n**Fixtures**\n- `yield` for teardown; the line after `yield` is the cleanup.\n- Default to function scope. Widen to `module`/`session` only for genuinely expensive resources.\n- `autouse` hides dependencies — use sparingly; prefer explicit injection.\n- `tmp_path` for temp files (auto-cleanup, `Path` API), not `tempfile`.\n\n**Parametrize**\n- `@pytest.mark.parametrize` over loops — distinct test IDs, filterable with `-k`.\n- Pass `ids=[...]` when params are objects or tuples; pytest already auto-names plain str/int/bool readably.\n\n**Config**\n- One config in `pyproject.toml` (`[tool.pytest.ini_options]`), not a separate `pytest.ini`.\n- `--strict-markers` so a typo'd marker fails instead of silently passing.\n- Register custom markers — e.g. `slow`, `@pytest.mark.unit`, `@pytest.mark.integration` — so `--strict-markers` catches a typo.\n- Coverage locally: `pytest --cov=src --cov-report=term-missing` — the missing-line report is the point; a bare percentage is not actionable.\n\n**Async (pytest-asyncio)**\n- Default mode is `strict`: an async test with no `@pytest.mark.asyncio` is silently not collected. Set `asyncio_mode = \"auto\"` in `[tool.pytest.ini_options]` to drop the per-test marker.\n- Use `@pytest_asyncio.fixture` for async fixtures in strict mode.\n\n\nFILE tests/tools/backup/progress_cli_cases.py\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nimport sys\nimport time\nfrom collections.abc import Iterator\nfrom io import StringIO\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport pytest\nfrom buvis.pybase.adapters import console\nfrom rich.console import Console\nfrom rich.text import Text\n\nimport backup.cli as backup_cli\nfrom backup.capabilities import CAPABILITIES\nfrom backup.config import BackupConfig, BackupInstance\nfrom backup.runner import Runner\nfrom backup.step_result import PlanEntry, ProgressEvent, StepResult\n\n\nclass StatusRecorder:\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\n        self.created: list[str] = []\n        self.events: list[tuple[str, object]] = []\n        self.current = \"\"\n        self.running = False\n        self.interrupt = False\n\n    def status(self, message: str) -> StatusRecorder:\n        self.created.append(message)\n        return self\n\n    def start(self) -> None:\n        self.running = True\n        self.events.append((\"start\", self.current))\n\n    def stop(self) -> None:\n        self.running = False\n        self.events.append((\"stop\", self.current))\n\n    def update(self, message: Text, **kwargs: object) -> None:\n        assert isinstance(message, Text)\n        self.current = message.plain\n        self.events.append((\"update\", self.current))\n        if self.interrupt:\n            self.interrupt = False\n            raise KeyboardInterrupt\n\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef cli_display(monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch) -> tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO]:\n    stream = StringIO()\n    monkeypatch.setattr(console, \"console\", Console(file=stream, width=240, color_system=None))\n    recorder = StatusRecorder()\n    monkeypatch.setattr(console, \"status\", recorder.status)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(sys.stdout, \"isatty\", lambda: True)\n    return recorder, stream\n\n\nclass ControlledCapability:\n    inputs: dict[str, object] = {}\n\n    def __init__(self, results: dict[str, StepResult], *, progress: bool = True) -> None:\n        self.results = results\n        self.progress = progress\n        self.closed: list[str] = []\n\n    def plan(self, **kwargs: object) -> PlanEntry:\n        label = str(kwargs[\"label\"])\n        return PlanEntry(label, f\"/source/{label}\", f\"/out/{label}.tar.gz\", \"run\", \"\", False)\n\n    def run(self, **kwargs: object) -> Iterator[StepResult]:\n        label = str(kwargs[\"label\"])\n        try:\n            callback = kwargs.get(\"progress\")\n            if self.progress and callable(callback):\n                callback(ProgressEvent(label, \"archiving\", 7, 19))\n                callback(ProgressEvent(label, \"finalizing\", 19, 19))\n            yield self.results[label]\n        finally:\n            self.closed.append(label)\n\n\ndef controlled_plan(\n    monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\n    results: list[StepResult],\n    *,\n    progress: bool = True,\n) -> tuple[BackupConfig, list[tuple[str, BackupInstance]], ControlledCapability]:\n    capability = ControlledCapability({result.label: result for result in results}, progress=progress)\n    monkeypatch.setitem(CAPABILITIES, \"cli-progress-fixture\", capability)\n    instances = {result.label: BackupInstance(use=\"cli-progress-fixture\") for result in results}\n    return BackupConfig(instances=instances), list(instances.items()), capability\n\n\ndef result_lines() -> list[StepResult]:\n    return [\n        StepResult(\"docs\", True, \"first archive ready\"),\n        StepResult(\"docs-old\", False, \"second archive denied\"),\n        StepResult(\"optional\", True, \"optional source absent\", skipped=True),\n    ]\n\n\nclass TestCliProgressFormat:\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\n        \"event,elapsed,expected\",\n        [\n            (ProgressEvent(\"docs\", \"archiving\", 37, 100), 65.9, \"docs archiving [37%] 1:05\"),\n            (ProgressEvent(\"docs-old\", \"archiving\", 7, 19), 9.9, \"docs-old archiving [36%] 0:09\"),\n            (ProgressEvent(\"docs\", \"archiving\", 100, 100), 3605, \"docs archiving [99%] 60:05\"),\n            (ProgressEvent(\"docs-old\", \"archiving\", 200, 100), -3, \"docs-old archiving [99%] 0:00\"),\n            (ProgressEvent(\"git\", \"scanning\", None, None), 2, \"git scanning 0:02\"),\n            (ProgressEvent(\"git-old\", \"archiving\", None, 700), 120, \"git-old archiving 2:00\"),\n            (ProgressEvent(\"git\", \"archiving\", 7, None), 61, \"git archiving 1:01\"),\n            (ProgressEvent(\"git-old\", \"archiving\", 0, 0), 59, \"git-old archiving 0:59\"),\n            (ProgressEvent(\"git\", \"archiving\", 0, -1), 0, \"git archiving 0:00\"),\n            (ProgressEvent(\"git\", \"finalizing\", 7, 19), 120, \"git finalizing 2:00\"),\n            (ProgressEvent(\"git-old\", \"finalizing\", 100, 100), 3661, \"git-old finalizing 61:01\"),\n            (ProgressEvent(\"\", \"scanning\", None, None), -0.5, \" scanning 0:00\"),\n        ],\n    )\n    def test_format_uses_input_byte_floor_caps_and_unbounded_minutes(\n        self,\n        event: ProgressEvent,\n        elapsed: float,\n        expected: str,\n    ) -> None:\n        assert backup_cli._format_progress(event, elapsed) == expected\n\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\n        \"done,total,percent\",\n        [(25, 100, 25), (1, 3, 33), (2, 7, 28), (13, 29, 44), (47, 64, 73), (1001, 4096, 24)],\n    )\n    def test_format_percentage_handles_varied_byte_ratios(self, done: int, total: int, percent: int) -> None:\n        event = ProgressEvent(\"arbitrary\", \"archiving\", done, total)\n        assert backup_cli._format_progress(event, 65) == f\"arbitrary archiving [{percent}%] 1:05\"\n\n\nclass TestCliLiveProgress:\n    def test_cli_three_active_labels_preserve_order_and_elapsed_across_phase_changes(\n        self,\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\n    ) -> None:\n        recorder, _ = cli_display\n        clock = [100.0]\n        monkeypatch.setattr(time, \"monotonic\", lambda: clock[0])\n        live = backup_cli._LiveProgress()\n        try:\n            live.on_progress(ProgressEvent(\"docs\", \"scanning\", None, None))\n            clock[0] = 130.0\n            live.on_progress(ProgressEvent(\"docs-old\", \"scanning\", None, None))\n            clock[0] = 160.0\n            live.on_progress(ProgressEvent(\"photos\", \"scanning\", None, None))\n            clock[0] = 165.0\n            live.on_progress(ProgressEvent(\"docs\", \"archiving\", 25, 100))\n            assert recorder.current == (\"docs archiving [25%] 1:05 | docs-old scanning 0:35 | photos scanning 0:05\")\n        finally:\n            live.close()\n\n    def test_cli_status_preserves_first_seen_time_order_and_exact_labels(\n        self,\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\n    ) -> None:\n        recorder, _ = cli_display\n        clock = [100.0]\n        monkeypatch.setattr(time, \"monotonic\", lambda: clock[0])\n        live = backup_cli._LiveProgress()\n        live.refresh()\n        live.finish(\"docs\")\n        assert recorder.created == []\n        live.on_progress(ProgressEvent(\"[red]docs\", \"scanning\", None, None))\n        clock[0] = 165.0\n        live.on_progress(ProgressEvent(\"[red]docs-old\", \"archiving\", 7, 19))\n        clock[0] = 170.0\n        live.on_progress(ProgressEvent(\"[red]docs\", \"finalizing\", 19, 19))\n        assert recorder.current == \"[red]docs finalizing 1:10 | [red]docs-old archiving [36%] 0:05\"\n        live.finish(\"docs\")\n        assert recorder.current.startswith(\"[red]docs finalizing 1:10 | \")\n        live.finish(\"[red]docs\")\n        assert recorder.current == \"[red]docs-old archiving [36%] 0:05\"\n        live.finish(\"[red]docs\")\n        assert recorder.running is True\n        live.finish(\"[red]docs-old\")\n        assert recorder.running is False\n        clock[0] = 180.0\n        live.on_progress(ProgressEvent(\"[red]docs\", \"archiving\", 3, 7))\n        assert recorder.current == \"[red]docs archiving [42%] 0:00\"\n        live.close()\n        live.close()\n        assert recorder.created == [\"\"]\n        assert [name for name, _ in recorder.events].count(\"start\") == 2\n        assert [name for name, _ in recorder.events].count(\"stop\") == 2\n\n    def test_cli_real_rich_status_restarts_after_all_labels_finish(\n        self,\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\n    ) -> None:\n        stream = StringIO()\n        monkeypatch.setattr(console, \"console\", Console(file=stream, force_terminal=True, width=160))\n        statuses: list[object] = []\n        factory = console.status\n\n        def capture_status(message: str) -> object:\n            status = factory(message)\n            statuses.append(status)\n            return status\n\n        monkeypatch.setattr(console, \"status\", capture_status)\n        live = backup_cli._LiveProgress()\n        try:\n            live.on_progress(ProgressEvent(\"[red]docs\", \"archiving\", 7, 19))\n            live.finish(\"[red]docs\")\n            live.on_progress(ProgressEvent(\"[red]docs-old\", \"finalizing\", 19, 19))\n            live.finish(\"[red]docs-old\")\n        finally:\n            live.close()\n        output = stream.getvalue()\n        assert len(statuses) == 1\n        assert \"[red]docs archiving [36%]\" in output\n        assert \"[red]docs-old finalizing\" in output\n\n    def test_cli_interrupted_status_update_propagates_and_close_stops_spinner(\n        self,\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\n    ) -> None:\n        recorder, _ = cli_display\n        live = backup_cli._LiveProgress()\n        live.on_progress(ProgressEvent(\"docs\", \"scanning\", None, None))\n        recorder.interrupt = True\n        try:\n            with pytest.raises(KeyboardInterrupt):\n                live.on_progress(ProgressEvent(\"docs-old\", \"archiving\", 7, 19))\n        finally:\n            live.close()\n        assert recorder.running is False\n        assert \"docs-old archiving [36%]\" in recorder.current\n\n\nclass TestCliProgressRunPlan:\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"dry_run,verb\", [(False, \"archived\"), (True, \"previewed\")])\n    def test_cli_report_summary_counts_each_outcome_and_describes_dry_run(\n        self,\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\n        dry_run: bool,\n        verb: str,\n    ) -> None:\n        _, stream = cli_display\n        assert backup_cli._report_steps(result_lines(), dry_run=dry_run) is True\n        assert stream.getvalue().splitlines()[-1].endswith(f\"{verb} 1, skipped 1, failed 1\")\n\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\n        \"result,marker\",\n        [\n            (StepResult(\"docs\", True, \"first archive ready\"), \"✔\"),\n            (StepResult(\"optional\", True, \"optional source absent\", skipped=True), \"⚠\"),\n            (StepResult(\"docs-old\", False, \"second archive denied\"), \"✘\"),\n        ],\n    )\n    def test_cli_result_output_uses_the_outcome_severity(\n        self,\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\n        result: StepResult,\n        marker: str,\n    ) -> None:\n        _, stream = cli_display\n        backup_cli._report_steps([result])\n        lines = [line for line in stream.getvalue().splitlines() if result.message in line]\n        assert len(lines) == 1\n        assert lines[0].lstrip().startswith(marker)\n        assert result.label in lines[0]\n\n    def test_cli_skipped_success_keeps_success_exit_and_skip_count(\n        self,\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\n    ) -> None:\n        _, stream = cli_display\n        result = StepResult(\"optional\", True, \"optional source absent\", skipped=True)\n        assert backup_cli._report_steps([result]) is False\n        assert stream.getvalue().splitlines()[-1].endswith(\"archived 0, skipped 1, failed 0\")\n\n    def test_cli_live_runner_tick_refreshes_elapsed_without_new_progress(\n        self,\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\n    ) -> None:\n        recorder, _ = cli_display\n        cfg, plan, capability = controlled_plan(monkeypatch, [StepResult(\"docs\", True, \"ready\")], progress=False)\n        clock = [100.0]\n        monkeypatch.setattr(time, \"monotonic\", lambda: clock[0])\n        refreshed: list[str] = []\n        original = Runner.__init__\n\n        def initialize(runner: Runner, *args: object, **kwargs: object) -> None:\n            original(runner, *args, **kwargs)\n            progress, tick = kwargs.get(\"on_progress\"), kwargs.get(\"on_tick\")\n            assert callable(progress)\n            assert callable(tick)\n            progress(ProgressEvent(\"docs\", \"scanning\", None, None))\n            clock[0] = 165.0\n            tick()\n            refreshed.append(recorder.current)\n\n        monkeypatch.setattr(Runner, \"__init__\", initialize)\n        assert backup_cli._run_plan(cfg, plan, dry_run=False, plan_only=False, jobs=1) is False\n        assert refreshed == [\"docs scanning 1:05\"]\n        assert capability.closed == [\"docs\"]\n        assert recorder.running is False\n\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"option\", [\"--quiet\", \"--list\", \"--show-excludes\"])\n    def test_cli_quiet_and_early_returns_never_create_live_status(\n        self,\n        tmp_path: Path,\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\n        option: str,\n    ) -> None:\n        recorder, stream = cli_display\n        source = tmp_path / \"source\"\n        source.mkdir()\n        (source / \"payload\").write_bytes(b\"actual CLI archive\")\n        out = tmp_path / \"result.tar.gz\"\n        config = tmp_path / \"buvis-backup.yaml\"\n        config.write_text(\n            json.dumps(\n                {\n                    \"excludes\": [\"private-cache\"],\n                    \"instances\": {\n                        \"docs\": {\n                            \"use\": \"tar-archive\",\n                            \"with\": {\n                                \"source\": str(source),\n                                \"out\": str(out),\n                                \"engine\": \"python-tarfile\",\n                            },\n                        }\n                    },\n                }\n            ),\n            encoding=\"utf-8\",\n        )\n        args = [\"--config-dir\", str(tmp_path), \"--config\", str(config)]\n        args += [option, \"docs\"] if option == \"--show-excludes\" else [\"--only\", \"docs\", option]\n        backup_cli.cli.main(args=args, standalone_mode=False)\n        assert recorder.created == []\n        assert out.exists() is (option == \"--quiet\")\n        output = stream.getvalue()\n        if option == \"--quiet\":\n            assert \"docs\" in output\n            assert \"archived\" in output\n        elif option == \"--show-excludes\":\n            assert \"private-cache\" in output\n        else:\n            assert \"docs\" in output\n\n    def test_cli_report_retries_pending_result_after_interrupt_without_duplicate_counts(\n        self,\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\n    ) -> None:\n        _, stream = cli_display\n        results = result_lines()\n        assert backup_cli._report_steps(results) is True\n        expected = stream.getvalue()\n        stream.seek(0)\n        stream.truncate()\n        delivered: list[StepResult] = []\n        interrupts: list[bool] = []\n\n        def before_result(step: StepResult) -> None:\n            delivered.append(step)\n            if len(delivered) == 1:\n                raise KeyboardInterrupt\n\n        assert (\n            backup_cli._report_steps(\n                iter(results),\n                on_interrupt=lambda: interrupts.append(True),\n                on_result=before_result,\n            )\n            is True\n        )\n        assert delivered == [results[0], *results]\n        assert interrupts == [True]\n        assert stream.getvalue() == expected\n\n    def test_cli_result_callback_error_is_surfaced_before_printing_result(\n        self,\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\n    ) -> None:\n        _, stream = cli_display\n\n        def fail_render(step: StepResult) -> None:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"cannot render {step.label}\")\n\n        with pytest.raises(RuntimeError, match=\"cannot render docs-old\"):\n            backup_cli._report_steps([StepResult(\"docs-old\", False, \"not printed\")], on_result=fail_render)\n        assert \"not printed\" not in stream.getvalue()\n\n    def test_cli_interrupted_live_run_closes_capability_and_status_before_exit_130(\n        self,\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\n    ) -> None:\n        recorder, stream = cli_display\n        cfg, plan, capability = controlled_plan(monkeypatch, result_lines())\n        recorder.interrupt = True\n        with pytest.raises(SystemExit) as caught:\n            backup_cli._run_plan(cfg, plan, dry_run=False, plan_only=False, jobs=1)\n        assert caught.value.code == 130\n        assert recorder.running is False\n        assert recorder.created == [\"\"]\n        assert capability.closed\n        assert set(capability.closed) <= {label for label, _ in plan}\n        assert \"interrupted:\" in stream.getvalue()\n\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"tty,quiet\", [(False, False), (True, True), (False, True)])\n    def test_no_live_output_when_not_a_tty_or_quiet(\n        self,\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\n        tty: bool,\n        quiet: bool,\n    ) -> None:\n        recorder, stream = cli_display\n        results = result_lines()\n        cfg, plan, capability = controlled_plan(monkeypatch, results)\n        monkeypatch.setattr(sys.stdout, \"isatty\", lambda: tty)\n        expected_failure = backup_cli._report_steps(results)\n        expected = stream.getvalue()\n        stream.seek(0)\n        stream.truncate()\n        failed = backup_cli._run_plan(cfg, plan, dry_run=False, plan_only=False, jobs=1, quiet=quiet)\n        assert failed is expected_failure is True\n        assert stream.getvalue() == expected\n        for result in results:\n            assert result.message in expected\n        assert len(expected.splitlines()) > len(results)\n        assert recorder.created == []\n        assert sorted(capability.closed) == sorted(result.label for result in results)\n\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\n        \"dry_run,plan_only,quiet,tty\",\n        [\n            (False, False, True, True),\n            (False, False, False, False),\n            (True, False, False, True),\n            (False, True, False, True),\n        ],\n    )\n    def test_cli_disabled_modes_pass_no_progress_or_tick_callbacks_to_real_runner(\n        self,\n        tmp_path: Path,\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\n        dry_run: bool,\n        plan_only: bool,\n        quiet: bool,\n        tty: bool,\n    ) -> None:\n        recorder, _ = cli_display\n        source = tmp_path / \"src\"\n        source.mkdir()\n        (source / \"payload\").write_bytes(b\"source bytes\")\n        out = tmp_path / \"out.tar.gz\"\n        instance = BackupInstance(use=\"tar-archive\", with_={\"source\": str(source), \"out\": str(out)})\n        cfg = BackupConfig(instances={\"docs\": instance})\n        calls: list[dict[str, object]] = []\n        original = Runner.__init__\n\n        def initialize(runner: Runner, *args: object, **kwargs: object) -> None:\n            calls.append(kwargs)\n            original(runner, *args, **kwargs)\n\n        monkeypatch.setattr(Runner, \"__init__\", initialize)\n        monkeypatch.setattr(sys.stdout, \"isatty\", lambda: tty)\n        assert (\n            backup_cli._run_plan(\n                cfg,\n                [(\"docs\", instance)],\n                dry_run=dry_run,\n                plan_only=plan_only,\n                quiet=quiet,\n            )\n            is False\n        )\n        assert len(calls) == 1\n        assert calls[0].get(\"on_progress\") is None\n        assert calls[0].get(\"on_tick\") is None\n        assert recorder.created == []\n        assert out.exists() is (not dry_run and not plan_only)\n\n    def test_cli_live_run_removes_completed_labels_before_each_final_line(\n        self,\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\n    ) -> None:\n        recorder, stream = cli_display\n        results = result_lines()\n        cfg, plan, capability = controlled_plan(monkeypatch, results)\n        observations: list[tuple[str, str]] = []\n        write = stream.write\n\n        def observe_output(message: str) -> int:\n            for result in results:\n                if result.message in message:\n                    observations.append((result.label, recorder.current if recorder.running else \"\"))\n            return write(message)\n\n        monkeypatch.setattr(stream, \"write\", observe_output)\n        assert backup_cli._run_plan(cfg, plan, dry_run=False, plan_only=False, jobs=1) is True\n        assert [label for label, _ in observations] == [result.label for result in results]\n        for label, active in observations:\n            assert label not in [part.split(\" \", 1)[0] for part in active.split(\" | \")]\n        assert recorder.created == [\"\"]\n        assert recorder.running is False\n        assert sorted(capability.closed) == sorted(result.label for result in results)\n        output = stream.getvalue()\n        for result in results:\n            assert output.count(result.message) == 1\n\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\"kind\", [\"empty\", \"preflight-failure\", \"no-progress\"])\n    def test_cli_live_run_without_active_events_never_creates_status(\n        self,\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\n        kind: str,\n    ) -> None:\n        recorder, stream = cli_display\n        results = [] if kind == \"empty\" else [StepResult(\"docs-old\", False, \"source unavailable\")]\n        cfg, plan, _ = controlled_plan(monkeypatch, results, progress=False)\n        if kind == \"preflight-failure\":\n            bad = BackupInstance(use=\"cli-progress-fixture-missing\")\n            cfg, plan = BackupConfig(instances={\"docs\": bad}), [(\"docs\", bad)]\n        assert backup_cli._run_plan(cfg, plan, dry_run=False, plan_only=False) is (kind != \"empty\")\n        assert recorder.created == []\n        assert recorder.running is False\n        if kind == \"no-progress\":\n            assert \"source unavailable\" in stream.getvalue()\n\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":2583}},"started_at_ms":1793569442408,"completed_at_ms":1793569442408}}
+{"timestamp":"2026-11-01T21:44:02.456Z","ordinal":25,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a19911-ca98-73e3-9ca6-5357815ad27c","call_id":"call_262e4adb0f6041e49804104052e93ed9","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 0.2 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"{\"chunk_id\":\"f7e329\",\"wall_time_seconds\":0.000002583,\"exit_code\":0,\"original_token_count\":6836,\"output\":\"\\nFILE /Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-patterns/SKILL.md\\n---\\nname: python-patterns\\ndescription: Use when writing, reviewing, or refactoring Python code. Covers idioms, naming, traps, toolchain, and security. Triggers on Python file edits, \\\"pythonic\\\", \\\"PEP 8\\\", \\\"python best practices\\\", \\\"python idioms\\\", \\\"bandit\\\".\\ncompatibility: \\\"Portable standalone compatibility copy of the strunk plugin skill for agents without that plugin; Claude Code uses the namespaced plugin skill.\\\"\\n---\\n\\n# Python Patterns\\n\\nPick a side. These are the rulings, not a tutorial.\\n\\n## Idioms that earn their place\\n\\n| Rule | Why |\\n|------|-----|\\n| `X \\\\| Y`, not `Union[X, Y]` | 3.10+ runtime syntax; clearer. On 3.9 it parses only under `from __future__ import annotations` and still breaks `get_type_hints`/`isinstance` — keep `Optional`/`Union` if you support 3.9. |\\n| `Protocol`, not `ABC`, for duck typing | Structural typing; no inheritance you don't control. |\\n| `@dataclass(frozen=True)` for immutable records, plain `dataclass` only when you must mutate, `NamedTuple` for lightweight immutable rows | Pydantic only when you need validation. |\\n| `raise New(...) from e` | Marks the explicit cause. A bare `raise New()` still chains implicitly (\\\"During handling...\\\"); use `from None` to suppress. |\\n| `@functools.wraps` on every decorator | Without it the wrapper loses `__name__`, `__doc__`, signature. |\\n| `pathlib.Path`, not `os.path` | One object, no string surgery. |\\n\\n## Naming (PEP 8)\\n\\n`snake_case` for modules, functions, variables. `CapWords` for classes. `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE` for constants. Leading `_` for internal names.\\n\\n**Never name a `.py` file in kebab-case.** `my-script.py` is not importable (`import my-script` is a `SyntaxError`). Kebab-case belongs only in the `pyproject.toml` distribution name and the CLI command, both of which map to a `snake_case` module.\\n\\n## Traps\\n\\n```python\\n# Mutable default argument — shared across calls\\ndef bad(items=[]): ...\\ndef good(items=None):\\n    items = [] if items is None else items\\n\\n# Bare except — swallows SystemExit, KeyboardInterrupt\\ntry: ...\\nexcept Exception as e: ...        # name the exception\\n\\n# __slots__ kills __dict__ and dynamic attributes — use only on fixed,\\n# memory-sensitive classes you won't extend.\\n\\n# __double_leading is name-mangled to _Class__double_leading.\\n# Surprises you in subclasses, pickling, and monkey-patching.\\n\\nif value is None: ...             # never == None\\n```\\n\\nAvoid `from module import *`. Use `isinstance`, never `type(x) ==`.\\n\\n## Toolchain\\n\\n**black** to format, **isort** for imports, **ruff** to lint. Type annotations on every function signature — no exceptions for \\\"obvious\\\" returns.\\n\\n## Resources and laziness\\n\\nContext managers (`with`) for anything holding a resource. Generators for lazy iteration over anything you would otherwise materialize into a list.\\n\\n## Security\\n\\n- Read secrets with `os.environ[\\\"API_KEY\\\"]`, never `.get()` — a missing secret must raise `KeyError` at startup, not surface as `None` at request time.\\n- `python-dotenv` loads a local `.env` in development only. Never commit one.\\n- `bandit -r src/` for static security analysis.\\n\\n\\nFILE /Users/bob/.agents/skills/python-testing/SKILL.md\\n---\\nname: python-testing\\ndescription: Use when writing, fixing, or reviewing Python tests with pytest. Covers TDD, fixtures, mocking, parametrization, coverage. Triggers on \\\"pytest\\\", \\\"python test\\\", \\\"conftest\\\", \\\"pytest.mark\\\", \\\"parametrize\\\", \\\"pytest fixture\\\", \\\"python mock\\\".\\ncompatibility: \\\"Portable standalone compatibility copy of the strunk plugin skill for agents without that plugin; Claude Code uses the namespaced plugin skill.\\\"\\n---\\n\\n# Python Testing\\n\\nTDD: write the failing test (RED), make it pass (GREEN), refactor. One behavior per test. No logic in tests. Coverage target 80%, higher on critical paths.\\n\\n## Rulings\\n\\n**Mocking**\\n- Patch where the name is *used*, not where it's defined: `@patch(\\\"myapp.service.requests\\\")`, not `@patch(\\\"requests\\\")`.\\n- `autospec=True` so the mock rejects calls the real API would reject.\\n- Mock at the boundary (I/O, network, clock). Never mock the thing under test.\\n- Async: assert with `assert_awaited_once()`, not `assert_called_once()`.\\n\\n**Fixtures**\\n- `yield` for teardown; the line after `yield` is the cleanup.\\n- Default to function scope. Widen to `module`/`session` only for genuinely expensive resources.\\n- `autouse` hides dependencies — use sparingly; prefer explicit injection.\\n- `tmp_path` for temp files (auto-cleanup, `Path` API), not `tempfile`.\\n\\n**Parametrize**\\n- `@pytest.mark.parametrize` over loops — distinct test IDs, filterable with `-k`.\\n- Pass `ids=[...]` when params are objects or tuples; pytest already auto-names plain str/int/bool readably.\\n\\n**Config**\\n- One config in `pyproject.toml` (`[tool.pytest.ini_options]`), not a separate `pytest.ini`.\\n- `--strict-markers` so a typo'd marker fails instead of silently passing.\\n- Register custom markers — e.g. `slow`, `@pytest.mark.unit`, `@pytest.mark.integration` — so `--strict-markers` catches a typo.\\n- Coverage locally: `pytest --cov=src --cov-report=term-missing` — the missing-line report is the point; a bare percentage is not actionable.\\n\\n**Async (pytest-asyncio)**\\n- Default mode is `strict`: an async test with no `@pytest.mark.asyncio` is silently not collected. Set `asyncio_mode = \\\"auto\\\"` in `[tool.pytest.ini_options]` to drop the per-test marker.\\n- Use `@pytest_asyncio.fixture` for async fixtures in strict mode.\\n\\n\\nFILE tests/tools/backup/progress_cli_cases.py\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\n\\nimport json\\nimport sys\\nimport time\\nfrom collections.abc import Iterator\\nfrom io import StringIO\\nfrom pathlib import Path\\n\\nimport pytest\\nfrom buvis.pybase.adapters import console\\nfrom rich.console import Console\\nfrom rich.text import Text\\n\\nimport backup.cli as backup_cli\\nfrom backup.capabilities import CAPABILITIES\\nfrom backup.config import BackupConfig, BackupInstance\\nfrom backup.runner import Runner\\nfrom backup.step_result import PlanEntry, ProgressEvent, StepResult\\n\\n\\nclass StatusRecorder:\\n    def __init__(self) -> None:\\n        self.created: list[str] = []\\n        self.events: list[tuple[str, object]] = []\\n        self.current = \\\"\\\"\\n        self.running = False\\n        self.interrupt = False\\n\\n    def status(self, message: str) -> StatusRecorder:\\n        self.created.append(message)\\n        return self\\n\\n    def start(self) -> None:\\n        self.running = True\\n        self.events.append((\\\"start\\\", self.current))\\n\\n    def stop(self) -> None:\\n        self.running = False\\n        self.events.append((\\\"stop\\\", self.current))\\n\\n    def update(self, message: Text, **kwargs: object) -> None:\\n        assert isinstance(message, Text)\\n        self.current = message.plain\\n        self.events.append((\\\"update\\\", self.current))\\n        if self.interrupt:\\n            self.interrupt = False\\n            raise KeyboardInterrupt\\n\\n\\n@pytest.fixture\\ndef cli_display(monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch) -> tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO]:\\n    stream = StringIO()\\n    monkeypatch.setattr(console, \\\"console\\\", Console(file=stream, width=240, color_system=None))\\n    recorder = StatusRecorder()\\n    monkeypatch.setattr(console, \\\"status\\\", recorder.status)\\n    monkeypatch.setattr(sys.stdout, \\\"isatty\\\", lambda: True)\\n    return recorder, stream\\n\\n\\nclass ControlledCapability:\\n    inputs: dict[str, object] = {}\\n\\n    def __init__(self, results: dict[str, StepResult], *, progress: bool = True) -> None:\\n        self.results = results\\n        self.progress = progress\\n        self.closed: list[str] = []\\n\\n    def plan(self, **kwargs: object) -> PlanEntry:\\n        label = str(kwargs[\\\"label\\\"])\\n        return PlanEntry(label, f\\\"/source/{label}\\\", f\\\"/out/{label}.tar.gz\\\", \\\"run\\\", \\\"\\\", False)\\n\\n    def run(self, **kwargs: object) -> Iterator[StepResult]:\\n        label = str(kwargs[\\\"label\\\"])\\n        try:\\n            callback = kwargs.get(\\\"progress\\\")\\n            if self.progress and callable(callback):\\n                callback(ProgressEvent(label, \\\"archiving\\\", 7, 19))\\n                callback(ProgressEvent(label, \\\"finalizing\\\", 19, 19))\\n            yield self.results[label]\\n        finally:\\n            self.closed.append(label)\\n\\n\\ndef controlled_plan(\\n    monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\\n    results: list[StepResult],\\n    *,\\n    progress: bool = True,\\n) -> tuple[BackupConfig, list[tuple[str, BackupInstance]], ControlledCapability]:\\n    capability = ControlledCapability({result.label: result for result in results}, progress=progress)\\n    monkeypatch.setitem(CAPABILITIES, \\\"cli-progress-fixture\\\", capability)\\n    instances = {result.label: BackupInstance(use=\\\"cli-progress-fixture\\\") for result in results}\\n    return BackupConfig(instances=instances), list(instances.items()), capability\\n\\n\\ndef result_lines() -> list[StepResult]:\\n    return [\\n        StepResult(\\\"docs\\\", True, \\\"first archive ready\\\"),\\n        StepResult(\\\"docs-old\\\", False, \\\"second archive denied\\\"),\\n        StepResult(\\\"optional\\\", True, \\\"optional source absent\\\", skipped=True),\\n    ]\\n\\n\\nclass TestCliProgressFormat:\\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\\n        \\\"event,elapsed,expected\\\",\\n        [\\n            (ProgressEvent(\\\"docs\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", 37, 100), 65.9, \\\"docs archiving [37%] 1:05\\\"),\\n            (ProgressEvent(\\\"docs-old\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", 7, 19), 9.9, \\\"docs-old archiving [36%] 0:09\\\"),\\n            (ProgressEvent(\\\"docs\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", 100, 100), 3605, \\\"docs archiving [99%] 60:05\\\"),\\n            (ProgressEvent(\\\"docs-old\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", 200, 100), -3, \\\"docs-old archiving [99%] 0:00\\\"),\\n            (ProgressEvent(\\\"git\\\", \\\"scanning\\\", None, None), 2, \\\"git scanning 0:02\\\"),\\n            (ProgressEvent(\\\"git-old\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", None, 700), 120, \\\"git-old archiving 2:00\\\"),\\n            (ProgressEvent(\\\"git\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", 7, None), 61, \\\"git archiving 1:01\\\"),\\n            (ProgressEvent(\\\"git-old\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", 0, 0), 59, \\\"git-old archiving 0:59\\\"),\\n            (ProgressEvent(\\\"git\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", 0, -1), 0, \\\"git archiving 0:00\\\"),\\n            (ProgressEvent(\\\"git\\\", \\\"finalizing\\\", 7, 19), 120, \\\"git finalizing 2:00\\\"),\\n            (ProgressEvent(\\\"git-old\\\", \\\"finalizing\\\", 100, 100), 3661, \\\"git-old finalizing 61:01\\\"),\\n            (ProgressEvent(\\\"\\\", \\\"scanning\\\", None, None), -0.5, \\\" scanning 0:00\\\"),\\n        ],\\n    )\\n    def test_format_uses_input_byte_floor_caps_and_unbounded_minutes(\\n        self,\\n        event: ProgressEvent,\\n        elapsed: float,\\n        expected: str,\\n    ) -> None:\\n        assert backup_cli._format_progress(event, elapsed) == expected\\n\\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\\n        \\\"done,total,percent\\\",\\n        [(25, 100, 25), (1, 3, 33), (2, 7, 28), (13, 29, 44), (47, 64, 73), (1001, 4096, 24)],\\n    )\\n    def test_format_percentage_handles_varied_byte_ratios(self, done: int, total: int, percent: int) -> None:\\n        event = ProgressEvent(\\\"arbitrary\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", done, total)\\n        assert backup_cli._format_progress(event, 65) == f\\\"arbitrary archiving [{percent}%] 1:05\\\"\\n\\n\\nclass TestCliLiveProgress:\\n    def test_cli_three_active_labels_preserve_order_and_elapsed_across_phase_changes(\\n        self,\\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\\n    ) -> None:\\n        recorder, _ = cli_display\\n        clock = [100.0]\\n        monkeypatch.setattr(time, \\\"monotonic\\\", lambda: clock[0])\\n        live = backup_cli._LiveProgress()\\n        try:\\n            live.on_progress(ProgressEvent(\\\"docs\\\", \\\"scanning\\\", None, None))\\n            clock[0] = 130.0\\n            live.on_progress(ProgressEvent(\\\"docs-old\\\", \\\"scanning\\\", None, None))\\n            clock[0] = 160.0\\n            live.on_progress(ProgressEvent(\\\"photos\\\", \\\"scanning\\\", None, None))\\n            clock[0] = 165.0\\n            live.on_progress(ProgressEvent(\\\"docs\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", 25, 100))\\n            assert recorder.current == (\\\"docs archiving [25%] 1:05 | docs-old scanning 0:35 | photos scanning 0:05\\\")\\n        finally:\\n            live.close()\\n\\n    def test_cli_status_preserves_first_seen_time_order_and_exact_labels(\\n        self,\\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\\n    ) -> None:\\n        recorder, _ = cli_display\\n        clock = [100.0]\\n        monkeypatch.setattr(time, \\\"monotonic\\\", lambda: clock[0])\\n        live = backup_cli._LiveProgress()\\n        live.refresh()\\n        live.finish(\\\"docs\\\")\\n        assert recorder.created == []\\n        live.on_progress(ProgressEvent(\\\"[red]docs\\\", \\\"scanning\\\", None, None))\\n        clock[0] = 165.0\\n        live.on_progress(ProgressEvent(\\\"[red]docs-old\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", 7, 19))\\n        clock[0] = 170.0\\n        live.on_progress(ProgressEvent(\\\"[red]docs\\\", \\\"finalizing\\\", 19, 19))\\n        assert recorder.current == \\\"[red]docs finalizing 1:10 | [red]docs-old archiving [36%] 0:05\\\"\\n        live.finish(\\\"docs\\\")\\n        assert recorder.current.startswith(\\\"[red]docs finalizing 1:10 | \\\")\\n        live.finish(\\\"[red]docs\\\")\\n        assert recorder.current == \\\"[red]docs-old archiving [36%] 0:05\\\"\\n        live.finish(\\\"[red]docs\\\")\\n        assert recorder.running is True\\n        live.finish(\\\"[red]docs-old\\\")\\n        assert recorder.running is False\\n        clock[0] = 180.0\\n        live.on_progress(ProgressEvent(\\\"[red]docs\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", 3, 7))\\n        assert recorder.current == \\\"[red]docs archiving [42%] 0:00\\\"\\n        live.close()\\n        live.close()\\n        assert recorder.created == [\\\"\\\"]\\n        assert [name for name, _ in recorder.events].count(\\\"start\\\") == 2\\n        assert [name for name, _ in recorder.events].count(\\\"stop\\\") == 2\\n\\n    def test_cli_real_rich_status_restarts_after_all_labels_finish(\\n        self,\\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\\n    ) -> None:\\n        stream = StringIO()\\n        monkeypatch.setattr(console, \\\"console\\\", Console(file=stream, force_terminal=True, width=160))\\n        statuses: list[object] = []\\n        factory = console.status\\n\\n        def capture_status(message: str) -> object:\\n            status = factory(message)\\n            statuses.append(status)\\n            return status\\n\\n        monkeypatch.setattr(console, \\\"status\\\", capture_status)\\n        live = backup_cli._LiveProgress()\\n        try:\\n            live.on_progress(ProgressEvent(\\\"[red]docs\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", 7, 19))\\n            live.finish(\\\"[red]docs\\\")\\n            live.on_progress(ProgressEvent(\\\"[red]docs-old\\\", \\\"finalizing\\\", 19, 19))\\n            live.finish(\\\"[red]docs-old\\\")\\n        finally:\\n            live.close()\\n        output = stream.getvalue()\\n        assert len(statuses) == 1\\n        assert \\\"[red]docs archiving [36%]\\\" in output\\n        assert \\\"[red]docs-old finalizing\\\" in output\\n\\n    def test_cli_interrupted_status_update_propagates_and_close_stops_spinner(\\n        self,\\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\\n    ) -> None:\\n        recorder, _ = cli_display\\n        live = backup_cli._LiveProgress()\\n        live.on_progress(ProgressEvent(\\\"docs\\\", \\\"scanning\\\", None, None))\\n        recorder.interrupt = True\\n        try:\\n            with pytest.raises(KeyboardInterrupt):\\n                live.on_progress(ProgressEvent(\\\"docs-old\\\", \\\"archiving\\\", 7, 19))\\n        finally:\\n            live.close()\\n        assert recorder.running is False\\n        assert \\\"docs-old archiving [36%]\\\" in recorder.current\\n\\n\\nclass TestCliProgressRunPlan:\\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\\\"dry_run,verb\\\", [(False, \\\"archived\\\"), (True, \\\"previewed\\\")])\\n    def test_cli_report_summary_counts_each_outcome_and_describes_dry_run(\\n        self,\\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\\n        dry_run: bool,\\n        verb: str,\\n    ) -> None:\\n        _, stream = cli_display\\n        assert backup_cli._report_steps(result_lines(), dry_run=dry_run) is True\\n        assert stream.getvalue().splitlines()[-1].endswith(f\\\"{verb} 1, skipped 1, failed 1\\\")\\n\\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\\n        \\\"result,marker\\\",\\n        [\\n            (StepResult(\\\"docs\\\", True, \\\"first archive ready\\\"), \\\"✔\\\"),\\n            (StepResult(\\\"optional\\\", True, \\\"optional source absent\\\", skipped=True), \\\"⚠\\\"),\\n            (StepResult(\\\"docs-old\\\", False, \\\"second archive denied\\\"), \\\"✘\\\"),\\n        ],\\n    )\\n    def test_cli_result_output_uses_the_outcome_severity(\\n        self,\\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\\n        result: StepResult,\\n        marker: str,\\n    ) -> None:\\n        _, stream = cli_display\\n        backup_cli._report_steps([result])\\n        lines = [line for line in stream.getvalue().splitlines() if result.message in line]\\n        assert len(lines) == 1\\n        assert lines[0].lstrip().startswith(marker)\\n        assert result.label in lines[0]\\n\\n    def test_cli_skipped_success_keeps_success_exit_and_skip_count(\\n        self,\\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\\n    ) -> None:\\n        _, stream = cli_display\\n        result = StepResult(\\\"optional\\\", True, \\\"optional source absent\\\", skipped=True)\\n        assert backup_cli._report_steps([result]) is False\\n        assert stream.getvalue().splitlines()[-1].endswith(\\\"archived 0, skipped 1, failed 0\\\")\\n\\n    def test_cli_live_runner_tick_refreshes_elapsed_without_new_progress(\\n        self,\\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\\n    ) -> None:\\n        recorder, _ = cli_display\\n        cfg, plan, capability = controlled_plan(monkeypatch, [StepResult(\\\"docs\\\", True, \\\"ready\\\")], progress=False)\\n        clock = [100.0]\\n        monkeypatch.setattr(time, \\\"monotonic\\\", lambda: clock[0])\\n        refreshed: list[str] = []\\n        original = Runner.__init__\\n\\n        def initialize(runner: Runner, *args: object, **kwargs: object) -> None:\\n            original(runner, *args, **kwargs)\\n            progress, tick = kwargs.get(\\\"on_progress\\\"), kwargs.get(\\\"on_tick\\\")\\n            assert callable(progress)\\n            assert callable(tick)\\n            progress(ProgressEvent(\\\"docs\\\", \\\"scanning\\\", None, None))\\n            clock[0] = 165.0\\n            tick()\\n            refreshed.append(recorder.current)\\n\\n        monkeypatch.setattr(Runner, \\\"__init__\\\", initialize)\\n        assert backup_cli._run_plan(cfg, plan, dry_run=False, plan_only=False, jobs=1) is False\\n        assert refreshed == [\\\"docs scanning 1:05\\\"]\\n        assert capability.closed == [\\\"docs\\\"]\\n        assert recorder.running is False\\n\\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\\\"option\\\", [\\\"--quiet\\\", \\\"--list\\\", \\\"--show-excludes\\\"])\\n    def test_cli_quiet_and_early_returns_never_create_live_status(\\n        self,\\n        tmp_path: Path,\\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\\n        option: str,\\n    ) -> None:\\n        recorder, stream = cli_display\\n        source = tmp_path / \\\"source\\\"\\n        source.mkdir()\\n        (source / \\\"payload\\\").write_bytes(b\\\"actual CLI archive\\\")\\n        out = tmp_path / \\\"result.tar.gz\\\"\\n        config = tmp_path / \\\"buvis-backup.yaml\\\"\\n        config.write_text(\\n            json.dumps(\\n                {\\n                    \\\"excludes\\\": [\\\"private-cache\\\"],\\n                    \\\"instances\\\": {\\n                        \\\"docs\\\": {\\n                            \\\"use\\\": \\\"tar-archive\\\",\\n                            \\\"with\\\": {\\n                                \\\"source\\\": str(source),\\n                                \\\"out\\\": str(out),\\n                                \\\"engine\\\": \\\"python-tarfile\\\",\\n                            },\\n                        }\\n                    },\\n                }\\n            ),\\n            encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\",\\n        )\\n        args = [\\\"--config-dir\\\", str(tmp_path), \\\"--config\\\", str(config)]\\n        args += [option, \\\"docs\\\"] if option == \\\"--show-excludes\\\" else [\\\"--only\\\", \\\"docs\\\", option]\\n        backup_cli.cli.main(args=args, standalone_mode=False)\\n        assert recorder.created == []\\n        assert out.exists() is (option == \\\"--quiet\\\")\\n        output = stream.getvalue()\\n        if option == \\\"--quiet\\\":\\n            assert \\\"docs\\\" in output\\n            assert \\\"archived\\\" in output\\n        elif option == \\\"--show-excludes\\\":\\n            assert \\\"private-cache\\\" in output\\n        else:\\n            assert \\\"docs\\\" in output\\n\\n    def test_cli_report_retries_pending_result_after_interrupt_without_duplicate_counts(\\n        self,\\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\\n    ) -> None:\\n        _, stream = cli_display\\n        results = result_lines()\\n        assert backup_cli._report_steps(results) is True\\n        expected = stream.getvalue()\\n        stream.seek(0)\\n        stream.truncate()\\n        delivered: list[StepResult] = []\\n        interrupts: list[bool] = []\\n\\n        def before_result(step: StepResult) -> None:\\n            delivered.append(step)\\n            if len(delivered) == 1:\\n                raise KeyboardInterrupt\\n\\n        assert (\\n            backup_cli._report_steps(\\n                iter(results),\\n                on_interrupt=lambda: interrupts.append(True),\\n                on_result=before_result,\\n            )\\n            is True\\n        )\\n        assert delivered == [results[0], *results]\\n        assert interrupts == [True]\\n        assert stream.getvalue() == expected\\n\\n    def test_cli_result_callback_error_is_surfaced_before_printing_result(\\n        self,\\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\\n    ) -> None:\\n        _, stream = cli_display\\n\\n        def fail_render(step: StepResult) -> None:\\n            raise RuntimeError(f\\\"cannot render {step.label}\\\")\\n\\n        with pytest.raises(RuntimeError, match=\\\"cannot render docs-old\\\"):\\n            backup_cli._report_steps([StepResult(\\\"docs-old\\\", False, \\\"not printed\\\")], on_result=fail_render)\\n        assert \\\"not printed\\\" not in stream.getvalue()\\n\\n    def test_cli_interrupted_live_run_closes_capability_and_status_before_exit_130(\\n        self,\\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\\n    ) -> None:\\n        recorder, stream = cli_display\\n        cfg, plan, capability = controlled_plan(monkeypatch, result_lines())\\n        recorder.interrupt = True\\n        with pytest.raises(SystemExit) as caught:\\n            backup_cli._run_plan(cfg, plan, dry_run=False, plan_only=False, jobs=1)\\n        assert caught.value.code == 130\\n        assert recorder.running is False\\n        assert recorder.created == [\\\"\\\"]\\n        assert capability.closed\\n        assert set(capability.closed) <= {label for label, _ in plan}\\n        assert \\\"interrupted:\\\" in stream.getvalue()\\n\\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\\\"tty,quiet\\\", [(False, False), (True, True), (False, True)])\\n    def test_no_live_output_when_not_a_tty_or_quiet(\\n        self,\\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\\n        tty: bool,\\n        quiet: bool,\\n    ) -> None:\\n        recorder, stream = cli_display\\n        results = result_lines()\\n        cfg, plan, capability = controlled_plan(monkeypatch, results)\\n        monkeypatch.setattr(sys.stdout, \\\"isatty\\\", lambda: tty)\\n        expected_failure = backup_cli._report_steps(results)\\n        expected = stream.getvalue()\\n        stream.seek(0)\\n        stream.truncate()\\n        failed = backup_cli._run_plan(cfg, plan, dry_run=False, plan_only=False, jobs=1, quiet=quiet)\\n        assert failed is expected_failure is True\\n        assert stream.getvalue() == expected\\n        for result in results:\\n            assert result.message in expected\\n        assert len(expected.splitlines()) > len(results)\\n        assert recorder.created == []\\n        assert sorted(capability.closed) == sorted(result.label for result in results)\\n\\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\\n        \\\"dry_run,plan_only,quiet,tty\\\",\\n        [\\n            (False, False, True, True),\\n            (False, False, False, False),\\n            (True, False, False, True),\\n            (False, True, False, True),\\n        ],\\n    )\\n    def test_cli_disabled_modes_pass_no_progress_or_tick_callbacks_to_real_runner(\\n        self,\\n        tmp_path: Path,\\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\\n        dry_run: bool,\\n        plan_only: bool,\\n        quiet: bool,\\n        tty: bool,\\n    ) -> None:\\n        recorder, _ = cli_display\\n        source = tmp_path / \\\"src\\\"\\n        source.mkdir()\\n        (source / \\\"payload\\\").write_bytes(b\\\"source bytes\\\")\\n        out = tmp_path / \\\"out.tar.gz\\\"\\n        instance = BackupInstance(use=\\\"tar-archive\\\", with_={\\\"source\\\": str(source), \\\"out\\\": str(out)})\\n        cfg = BackupConfig(instances={\\\"docs\\\": instance})\\n        calls: list[dict[str, object]] = []\\n        original = Runner.__init__\\n\\n        def initialize(runner: Runner, *args: object, **kwargs: object) -> None:\\n            calls.append(kwargs)\\n            original(runner, *args, **kwargs)\\n\\n        monkeypatch.setattr(Runner, \\\"__init__\\\", initialize)\\n        monkeypatch.setattr(sys.stdout, \\\"isatty\\\", lambda: tty)\\n        assert (\\n            backup_cli._run_plan(\\n                cfg,\\n                [(\\\"docs\\\", instance)],\\n                dry_run=dry_run,\\n                plan_only=plan_only,\\n                quiet=quiet,\\n            )\\n            is False\\n        )\\n        assert len(calls) == 1\\n        assert calls[0].get(\\\"on_progress\\\") is None\\n        assert calls[0].get(\\\"on_tick\\\") is None\\n        assert recorder.created == []\\n        assert out.exists() is (not dry_run and not plan_only)\\n\\n    def test_cli_live_run_removes_completed_labels_before_each_final_line(\\n        self,\\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\\n    ) -> None:\\n        recorder, stream = cli_display\\n        results = result_lines()\\n        cfg, plan, capability = controlled_plan(monkeypatch, results)\\n        observations: list[tuple[str, str]] = []\\n        write = stream.write\\n\\n        def observe_output(message: str) -> int:\\n            for result in results:\\n                if result.message in message:\\n                    observations.append((result.label, recorder.current if recorder.running else \\\"\\\"))\\n            return write(message)\\n\\n        monkeypatch.setattr(stream, \\\"write\\\", observe_output)\\n        assert backup_cli._run_plan(cfg, plan, dry_run=False, plan_only=False, jobs=1) is True\\n        assert [label for label, _ in observations] == [result.label for result in results]\\n        for label, active in observations:\\n            assert label not in [part.split(\\\" \\\", 1)[0] for part in active.split(\\\" | \\\")]\\n        assert recorder.created == [\\\"\\\"]\\n        assert recorder.running is False\\n        assert sorted(capability.closed) == sorted(result.label for result in results)\\n        output = stream.getvalue()\\n        for result in results:\\n            assert output.count(result.message) == 1\\n\\n    @pytest.mark.parametrize(\\\"kind\\\", [\\\"empty\\\", \\\"preflight-failure\\\", \\\"no-progress\\\"])\\n    def test_cli_live_run_without_active_events_never_creates_status(\\n        self,\\n        monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch,\\n        cli_display: tuple[StatusRecorder, StringIO],\\n        kind: str,\\n    ) -> None:\\n        recorder, stream = cli_display\\n        results = [] if kind == \\\"empty\\\" else [StepResult(\\\"docs-old\\\", False, \\\"source unavailable\\\")]\\n        cfg, plan, _ = controlled_plan(monkeypatch, results, progress=False)\\n        if kind == \\\"preflight-failure\\\":